{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TypeTxSync","paragraph_zero_based":47544},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the synchronization reference type. For configurations by the eNB/gNB, only gnbEnb can be configured; and for pre-configuration or when this field is absent, the configuration is applicable for all synchronization reference types. ","paragraph_zero_based":47545},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ThresUE-Speed","paragraph_zero_based":47546},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates a UE absolute speed threshold.","paragraph_zero_based":47547},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47548},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":47549},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":47550},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CBR","paragraph_zero_based":47551},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, when the IE SL-PSSCH-TxParameters is present in SL-CBR-CommonTxConfigList, SL-UE-SelectedConfig, SIB12 or SidelinkPreconfigNR; otherwise the field is not present, need R.","paragraph_zero_based":47552},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47553},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-QoS-FlowIdentity","paragraph_zero_based":47554},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-QoS-FlowIdentity is used to identify a sidelink QoS flow.","paragraph_zero_based":47555},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-QoS-FlowIdentity information element","paragraph_zero_based":47556},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":47557},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-QOS-FLOWIDENTITY-START","paragraph_zero_based":47558},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47559},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-QoS-FlowIdentity-r16 ::=                    INTEGER (1..maxNrofSL-QFIs-r16)","paragraph_zero_based":47560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-QOS-FLOWIDENTITY-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":47562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":47563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-QoS-Profile","paragraph_zero_based":47565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-QoS-Profile is used to give the QoS parameters for a sidelink QoS flow. Need codes or conditions specified for SL-QoS-Profile do not apply, in case SL-QoS-Profile is included in SidelinkUEInformationNR.","paragraph_zero_based":47566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-QoS-Profile information element","paragraph_zero_based":47567}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0a306b978fdb29fb88cd94ff28f26c3242010552e745de9d32b93818533ac753","4146550ee50f5cf010e8262897956fffd00129db2d2d8698f1bc4d6fda201513","22092cdf09254b7cff4654ee92e27a79e0316dab81476cb2a24f09f3ffff59fd","27a1ddfe55410bb793a7da593565bb63dac419842b949eb7b017f5c48306c3d4","06f59c8d60ddea90d2a96f3fbbd8f34fdd8ca0e435d34b7d2c2c105676727f81","f2c609b15b17c98cbcb09defd7326c427600f0fc23930774c2e9324f4a81bf3f","32df8f2c68421c2a1ac642dd843a11d88f5aec13af130d8ff8cc8a41274a1bd1","4e7f4a66b77495f0fe709b9a96e0942eb268cac90cc6bcbd0704e4014f771e3d","d2a55eee57bf8034d33f3f04fe07a6dd8602c93af63925a26b1a8e7fae5d807c","2e5f05eb2f92f887fef90fa1f7c83f92b82d107d1dfd4be6b89b84a83c2f4500","7d88de8b8c5a7976eb35ef95c89eb1b38113422ab3c3b8fbe1e40b17586b1584","ec993095554dc0043ba4672ef1eb72f889da611ed84428