{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-QOS-PROFILE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":47592},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":47593},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47594},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-QoS-Profile field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":47595},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-GFBR","paragraph_zero_based":47596},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicate the guaranteed bit rate for a GBR QoS flow. The unit is: Kbit/s","paragraph_zero_based":47597},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MFBR","paragraph_zero_based":47598},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicate the maximum bit rate for a GBR QoS flow. The unit is: Kbit/s","paragraph_zero_based":47599},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PQI","paragraph_zero_based":47600},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates either the PQI for standardized PQI or non-standardized QoS parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":47601},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-Range","paragraph_zero_based":47602},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the range parameter of the Qos flow, as defined in clause 5.4.1.1.1, TS 23.287 [55]. It is present only for groupcast. The unit is meter.","paragraph_zero_based":47603},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47604},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PQI field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":47605},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-AveragingWindow","paragraph_zero_based":47606},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the Averaging Window for a QoS flow, and applies to GBR QoS flows only. Unit: ms. The default value of the IE is 2000ms.","paragraph_zero_based":47607},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MaxDataBurstVolume","paragraph_zero_based":47608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the Maximum Data Burst Volume for a QoS flow, and applies to delay critical GBR QoS flows only. Unit: byte.","paragraph_zero_based":47609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PacketDelayBudget","paragraph_zero_based":47610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the Packet Delay Budget for a QoS flow. Upper bound value for the delay that a packet may experience expressed in unit of 0.5ms.","paragraph_zero_based":47611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PacketErrorRate","paragraph_zero_based":47612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the Packet Error Rate for a QoS flow. The packet error rate is expressed as Scalar x 10-k where k is the Exponent.","paragraph_zero_based":47613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PriorityLevel","paragraph_zero_based":47614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the Priority Level for a QoS flow. Values ordered in decreasing order of priority, i.e. with 1 as the highest priority and 8 as the lowest priority.","paragraph_zero_based":47615}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ce4651e4d509574e47aabde404d56659fcb76e261044aa2b555b30a6017c82b3","36f36c216867ba21c8734321cd9a291beddaf62486d90c4079f4fdf4174cc277","e63d30aae65daf59e26a8b0d0eb046457d8ba5800fc8be6794b508f5bf06ebee","d2af6f2b37ccfa04757b8cb43876750c0aa68ed04e4e419088edc8f065ea614e","4002691413a89542ec1a6ca9b4060ad4bd8977cb4e81b8604cc759812867da15","bbe52993e9bfd3584278e32fb2d67d25a2c419c85076bf3c0c94e2abb49e6576","6620732044a0248430e6a0b7def7057e6eb40c6361a652cec8d1d0f17030944e","a7f8fa772c62eb36be095c38368aec6f5f569ef30b3d8c71ca1a7435dfc802ad","b65ddad1f5bd058d83efe4f3c9a8bf2116941696b12aa192a7fb2d5fc2703b9a","f9ef9ed82eb637a9b319a659cf9ef8766a