{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the probability with which the UE keeps the current resource when the resource reselection counter reaches zero for sensing based UE autonomous resource selection (see TS 38.321 [3]).","paragraph_zero_based":48816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PSSCH-TxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":48817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates PSSCH TX parameters such as MCS, sub-channel number, retransmission number, associated to different UE absolute speeds and different synchronization reference types for UE autonomous resource selection.","paragraph_zero_based":48818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ReselectAfter","paragraph_zero_based":48819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of consecutive skipped transmissions before triggering resource reselection for sidelink communication (see TS 38.321 [3]).","paragraph_zero_based":48820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-PrioritizationThres","paragraph_zero_based":48821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the UL priority threshold, which is used to determine whether SL TX is prioritized over UL TX, as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Network does not configure the sl-PrioritizationThres and the ul-PrioritizationThres to the UE separately.","paragraph_zero_based":48822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":48824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":48825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SIB12","paragraph_zero_based":48826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is optional present if included within SIB12, need R. Otherwise, the field is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":48827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"notSIB12","paragraph_zero_based":48828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is absent in SIB12. Otherwise, it is optional present, Need R","paragraph_zero_based":48829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-ZoneConfig","paragraph_zero_based":48831},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-ZoneConfig is used to configure the zone ID related parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":48832},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-ZoneConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":48833},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":48834},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-ZONECONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":48835},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48836},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-ZoneConfig-r16 ::=              SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":48837},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-ZoneLength-r16                  ENUMERATED { m5, m10, m20, m30, m40, m50, spare2, spare1},","paragraph_zero_based":48838},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":48839}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["206329147250b5e01d6c4d89e90b88c3df9fd14ea6ffcae1abd916c51a025204","c5aa3392e6ff35c878415673af82f7c6b1318ab3f4a9ebc97b3de8b304a749ca","a831b24bf6a783560a602c5736cc7278aa5df7bd9e60084ffb8fb1193e9106de","ddfcebe9507395ec6a7395f3f8a5d73d30716820d28aa502b1adb47df199f45e","0eceb55adf97000ad9acdc4577910539a978038370289285f9ca6df00a1cf0cb","5e0601ea83a5ebe69295f6f91e9a669eb1bb45b92f80263c2b8c752d13c85ad8","b406409f0dc5aab217a0452bca5bb9e5fae1201f6b2e9521f7d46746c1f86b3c","f6f5adbfa40d5a0bb5e55308621df24b03fc88293a3bbe2b20d12c69a2aaf007","c8b8863