{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ms0","paragraph_zero_based":52560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":52561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":52562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":52563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.1.2Void","paragraph_zero_based":52564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2Default radio configurations","paragraph_zero_based":52565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The following clauses only list default values for REL-15 parameters included in protocol version v15.3.0. For all fields introduced in a later protocol version, the default value is \"released\" or \"false\" unless explicitly specified otherwise. If the UE is to apply default configuration while it is configured with some critically extended fields, the UE shall apply the original version of those fields with only default values.","paragraph_zero_based":52566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:In general, the signalling should preferably support a \"release\" option for fields introduced after v15.3.0. The \"value not applicable\" should be used restrictively, mainly limited to for fields which value is relevant only if another field is set to a value other than its default.","paragraph_zero_based":52567},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:For parameters in ServingCellConfig, the default values are specified in the corresponding specification.","paragraph_zero_based":52568},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.1Default SRB configurations","paragraph_zero_based":52569},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters","paragraph_zero_based":52570},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Name","paragraph_zero_based":52571},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value","paragraph_zero_based":52572},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Semantics descr