{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2407525.zip::R2-2407525.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"0-3","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DL modulation scheme","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1) QPSK modulation","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2) 16QAM modulation","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3) 64QAM modulation for FR1","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"0-4","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UL modulation scheme","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1) QPSK modulation","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2) 16QAM modulation","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Therefore, DFT-S-OFDM should be considerred as an optional feature for NCR-MT, this is aligned with the below statement in current spec.  ","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2.23.1Mandatory NCR-MT features","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Table 4.2.23.1-1, Table 4.2.23.1-2 and Table 4.2.23.1-3 capture feature groups, which are mandatory for an NCR-MT.","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CA, MR-DC, handover (e.g. CHO, DAPS, CPAC, etc), unlicensed band, HPUE Duty cycle, MPR related UE features and corresponding capabilities are not supported by an NCR-MT. All other feature groups or components of the feature groups as captured in TR 38.822 [24] as well as capabilities specified in this specification are optional for an NCR-MT, unless indicated otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"However, because legacy NR UEs must support these two UL waveforms, thus no capability has been introduced for indicating the support of CP-OFDM or DFT-S-OFDM UL waveforms. Therefore, there is no way for a NCR-MT to report its support of DFT-S-OFDM for UL. ","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For IAB-MT, a separate optional capability (i.e. dft-S-OFDM-WaveformUL-IAB-r16) was introduced, so, for NCR-MT, the similar capability can also be introduced. ","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"“","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Introduce UE capability “ncr-dft-S-OFDM-WaveformUL-r18” for NCR-MT.","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":94},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted 5G architecture options:","paragraph_zero_based":95}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"abf11d476ccb1587c08fc50ad8cf7430b8fce456680c2264c98057397f1240ef","original_member_sha256":"e33c48f2a9a55345abc1b2b94edf844cc8aed534a8b393c4ffbc91820ad41bfc","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["487cd269c217996c38c04f7721accd57e8b9e07ba20d4437eb7097bfa1bbd6d1","53efcb572f40dbd6359661845f6c80b95146bb478bccd1eb219ad50c8212b8df","3b6c7edd820a3b44dc515c1f128632f4ed135d1b250c2424bce19b99b1e035c1","13cd918dfb64ad02feede77b7381546294de58514e1c6211ebd647019eae94ae","058c1312b01741c084a53e2c1a4cbcd7b78cf4523df0e9145298b4ccaaa62bc1","517b38a67c4b2ec36cac28ad2b018bfbd87cfcc9b75d8a99c54b58bd883c084b","5f1fbaa2a5279333223cced963e64bf9d9d339f0eb70ddec6ef39204bb02c3ed","95c1b092f380d081bc3b4738bcc9cfbecb83ac2f96c439bf3fd84ccf2d3f3e44","086a633c837578a2d5838397ba4b2869e71d578e5c93f4560e4617a69c1ef675","4e528ae1f99dad77e1e09c07ccfca729d42f9be573095bae7a7909