L_sha256":"10aa75fb96d1678a2599189670d49d37545c3896199d099d18db47b2dd37752f","original_member_sha256":"f4e322dc8c96fc8443fbf11d52da762bd2998773228fe0ec6e011261c1edc700","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["20e285f077227d22dd3b5981c8976f9d56ea5d88ffd7f790036b30e5d2c0b4a9","4328dbc2e9ed59984edad9da9f918a037222a8bc1d4a7f801e449d0bf4e71fd0","1b57abbb250ccf0e7dbcfaad8666dd22e39df29408dc1d6e61b3298df1a31533","dca27312d7a1517d19ed558671871fab25e9b549c607883b97a78f9f3628f08a","6d3fba1314de1001e3753ed4f16b9c74cdf0271805f61b17dcc5b42bd590842f","617785343afc34ff86d7085e070e5171c849cf65b766df069d11ae4921b43535","ef64cb158b3c2c7e7377f1b35278ac045036ac7993e6321b5b48767e6e15e5a5","cb9646e53a961acadd8b9d1cbe9977f71385aded0c0dd84e225defb7e8545ad8","a2f067725ab572fcc4bc1fef5b1bafc2fb55dfbfe071c00200782d1efc3b2bd5","48f27d1f338f2e6cabf1ff384625f9d1a5e67ab8190bf0af224f5e9fd5a2044d","c4809416473a41579300b3e517a5f45ab05af850f6be5fcb7294205cf90f7e6b","731cd85286f824ffc8ab15b3e076faaf16231b040ec58d5b982eb0b04411f518","fe4276ba86eaf32e2ed51b67e3c51006e25dcb2c4865dd063bc02fd31ecf7498","15446e336e26f8e8542354aaa67cefc1b9b0d8b4af76558f1b7e96594ab3e72b","032e9f858d3d59ab048f1c6847f25e5b233bb6ba0c88c96eee40690f328745ca","1ac810a1cab11c95a1df934fbe11d17d0c7b90f828c877e62a98a07ed58b7dfa","d33bdb3a02fea28de5eb95e389804aa2c5148a32030728b12c57c6dcd8b2b56f","b3f8ba76ec829a0eac6003bc8cbccaed17d41a62756dd1214cc8a7fa8c87c76d","ebb18e058d1fac3e0efc9941e530e6c9327f91af82e47a50969e70a111afea2a","740b3eefc4f7734a18ef9caf8d1a2b9a1a9ced0a2a20ec872f85a0d92009babd","dcb00a9e6c6c316c0088d2dc5f1b8ad2617b4424352762cd9029642ce44b55be","adf91afec1ef44a2388772bd7103ea6e4f36004e933a3b58dc00af5209fde022","500ae1e95311986e752b9be027e0c22a78d267c2f0de2c686523828721158b14","1cef444d894cdacbe559bb45e53c3b2ef7f77da82c45f0f24d784d4541645307"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[24,47],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2407566.zip::R2-2407566_CR for Correction on PHR for mTRP PUSCH repetition (R18).docx:p24"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2407566.zip::R2-2407566_CR for Correction on PHR for mTRP PUSCH repetition (R18).docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1. In TS 38.213, it is not clear whether/when one Type 3 PH value is provided for a serving cell configured with mTRP PUSCH repetition instead of two Type 1 PH values, while it is clearly specified that two Type 1 PH value is provided for the serving cell configured with mTRP PUSCH repetition. In addition, according to RAN1 reply LS (R1-2405619), RAN1 did not reach a consensus on whether/how the UE can report one Type 3 PH value instead of two Type 1 PH values.","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In order to avoid the ambiguity and to minize the specification impact, two Type 1 PH are always obtained for the serving cell configured with mTRP PUSCH repetition, if the MAC entity the serving cell belongs to is configured with twoPHRMode.","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2. In Enhanced Multiple Entry PHR for mTRP MAC CE, one or two Type 1 PH can be included for PCell. However, this is not specified correctly in the description.","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3. In Enhanced Multiple Entry PHR for mTRP MAC CE, Type 2 PH2 field for SpCell is not needed because Type 2 PH value for SpCell is included for E-UTRA MAC entity and the E-UTRA MAC entity is not configured twoPHRMode. Therefore, Type 2 PH2 field for SpCell should be removed. ","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":" ","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1. In 5.4.6, remove obtaining Type 3 PH for the case where a serving cell is configured with mTRP PUSCH repetition and the MAC entity the serving cell belongs to is configured with twoPHRMode.","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"10aa75fb96d1678a2599189670d49d37545c3896199d099d18db47b2dd37752f","original_member_sha256":"f4e322dc8c96fc8443fbf11d52da762bd2998773228fe0ec6e011261c1edc700","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e4ea5591218aa96d0cd407936b651eb165fb4c75e229dab64ec9de6be991cb96","2d00e3b1a82065155328ddd802c3d4a8ebff11f4a0d6da9ecf9b1e34dc8ebfc8","ba310ca4eb7ae80e30e816e1fc737877c4764e6d7c8b991e25d303f614a3a0be","761fa4d36b282591b5f5bb5ee554c6086f6eb9d5925f257d405f142f9e3a17e1","9ee3a8ef1b4d8b5d23ae68c79878f83d9a7ffdf02ec93cff53f7b1de6029f4d6","a2c41daa60c61e7f963026229e9e1437392aa174baf3dafb1a694156646211fe","b08252b53f111fda758564f01d6aeb287a86ceee9730eba0ca5fcf7c7dadb00e","5397ebe3cc2afa3393b897343a62f60e5b485315d8236802a715ec930f5cc336","9179ba236853e4a73f15d3d408619f0f62540850e6daa878c17cdc8a8f26dbb9","34212fc6f04370a4e535ce9cc41d8546dd1f377420e476f0306c144fd63998ef","16c8d70f7d429c511b56c375317337c5d5c75b5a185ec91bf088b77069963fb7","acd6206245de4b9556a4853ff1b8b41875944834aa76df6c7d72af763f365262","3c4c80e1e11044a4d07c2d065ab1badcf74a3b84af6435503a27154aade28f9b","78dd1ad85521a5ed8f6a35cf977e12d1664d834cba300e9a8dd91f3db7ee6a34","ba37a6f6cbeada800db48c61e597a71270d0aee26fe43a916b077232a48f5a49","46894119f72cb3be64704db6c82512aecd84747f8260ff6bb4cd726468100b66","df22d6a8cc41a0600d34db62426b0b20daabef4836e7b84e3b0beea10f456190","3d7d2c40038cdaa2785f7dd6848e4d0434f4cc2167ca7d2b6fc0badbd4b220aa","f60649edf342795e35659a2201c7f41550288b2c55acf5dc7176c708b14723d7","6fba9f5131646c628de148f92c02216a61a25ca6846c4dbb97a0758d9f91be57","8b24573e0133d1c5ee95e1377545628b16380b4d3d980bde5296376e8173041e","7423559940944ed0cc1fe176b76253cf9035dcdbfc0fac2f3e385feb311a2329","288cc60197c635a28716a1c3a9133085106b36b1009fb0a2849670c1b99dfd9f","bf4008da6e4679ba13aee6a5b8b6a81a76b35bb5d13b779b4495e62abb9259dd"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[48,71],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2407566.zip::R2-2407566_CR for Correction on PHR for mTRP PUSCH repetition (R18).docx:p48"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2407566.zip::R2-2407566_CR for Correction on PHR for mTRP PUSCH repetition (R18).docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 6.1.3.51, change \"Type X\" to \"Type 1\" for PH2 on Serving Cells.","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2. In 6.1.3.51, change \"a Type 1 PH field\" to \"one or multiple Type 1 PH field\".","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3. In 6.1.3.51, remove Type 2 PH 2 on SpCell in Figure 6.1.3.51-1 and Figure 6.1.3.51-2.","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted functionality: FeMIMO.","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-operability: ","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the network may not correctly decode Enhanced Multiple Entry PHR for mTRP MAC CE.","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network may not correctly decode Enhanced Muyltiple Entry PHR for mTRP MAC CE.","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE and the network may have different understanding on whether two Type 1 PH values or one Type 3 HP value is included in Enhanced Multiple Entry PHR for mTRP MAC CE, so there may be a misalignment between the UE and the network.","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Thus, the network may not decode Enhanced Multiple Entry PHR for mTRP MAC CE correctly.","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Clauses affected:","paragraph_zero_based":94},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.4.6, 6.1.3.51","paragraph_zero_based":95}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"10aa75fb96d1678a2599189670d49d37545c3896199d099d18db47b2dd37752f","original_member_sha256":"f4e322dc8c96fc8443fbf11d52da762bd2998773228fe0ec6e011261c1edc700","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["88491535a3f22b99b7e69bddaa9e987c5d251626b03254e796bdedf98452df45","ec1c802f9879725a0d61fdcf720bcccc5a419705d5c988d15261ae25a687d387","43e673cfd43c1f971434ee48afba53d9f9dd8ec125fddb363b9d9bd25a00b769","052b1b331038ba04b4c370bf8f8e3cb6d6568e95164006f78a88324681f20cc1","0dd82bbe68691028e732608aaa95d7757633eb4e89f9389e5324c785baa1a4ba","6404e8c3be407940466e5e923f5ce83771cdc359179e52e41d56a97b46e71ca9","3ef52a03e9bf60832710de9bc5b8b8f06d8698c7e269839a69f25319478cc4a6","37feec4d7f23d9f3257c04956ed1327ed737a2abe75bbbc96e94d20ed825f6de","5668e4db075e45d0c77370e434527ee6523ce2ab8ae7ed7dec35d29456f5a128","e43cc17c86ff836d938e03be7bae88493e7bb1f3d40cd81b0ae7570127a9abec","cef53aa47fef6ff1f40e054e4b20f3d9ebc91b80eba724c7ab8dadafcc1f1b91","bd5d391d28082f4ff39fcafcabb67543a769010ae1db01e0c7cfdbb443fcc072","7c8747ded4ee15187cfc2f1d4635b4312ad155bafdd1283a560face83bda7fe1","77404f754528ecd121ddb5d065d838df070695de43ce2d4165fe2b3af4e5ade7","23da18bbbcbc650fad7a07ef800