{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When cellBarredRedCap1Rx is set to \"barred\" and barringExemptEmergencyCall is present in SIB1, if the cell will not be treated as barred by the UE for any reason other than the cellBarredRedCap1Rx being set to \"barred\" (see TS 38.331 [3]), and cell selection criteria are fulfilled as defined in clause 5.2.3,","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The RedCap UE that supports barring exemption for emergency call (see TS 38.306 [24]) and only 1Rx branch shall treat this cell as an acceptable cell.","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When cellBarredRedCap2Rx is set to \"barred\" and barringExemptEmergencyCall is present in SIB1, if the cell will not be treated as barred by the UE for any reason other than the cellBarredRedCap2Rx being set to \"barred\" (see TS 38.331 [3]), and cell selection criteria are fulfilled as defined in clause 5.2.3,","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ceb2fed5ac41aa5a70361f6c6857a182e415c356d359a9f953135cf514892f5a","original_member_sha256":"315f0f255b36340f21e8203b9b979c7ecc29e421ee45b443dd903b4e229dd079","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9e729201b649496e10a49a3d74f815b2a18ddc989cb8eb0a841fdf24de033e4e","b3c598a2c3a78c0732b17f6599d62583c73ddfd68600356a31bdebc6f72d3756","f6111cb06d436714368086fba474d4152435671c25d54093b2c0cc9de9cc3d7e","d2710da83d6ac57837a883d4557544f663ad41e30744a18ecd7af7ed771787aa","f38696b8b67a74caf2ec3a632be35195b72a2fa7879e0c966530fce09cabba25","c658895c997655578c5e12b38a8fe722e42085e16e2698084c2f7e0d2607203d","de417fc553456dc45642abb92e84e5759e33801cb4894523ec0f1f863e7ab35d","ef7589365e0afce72272bf17d2be200280ab1ea8fd91c17592ddc7ae1b311ddb","4b7992f756a536e7ce3500cc2f96cc454bd6ce2225ba5e81eb9ed6f48b56d198","1283c17d29ba0798ca3d4127d8bebff94acb67fa9d785ce06c243c0562960cd7","1b7eaa2c8b99931f970524881d10e0ab204e9deafdf2753107ad38f4fa7cdabe","c75ec9d141d4b2fe3cef16877a8b8faacaaaf13b799b3636dc66a0ec3e621f76","1e4b555cf7dc806373ded324e30b7b98e56200545cb982c9c62a681ea9dc8265","6f4590eb938870111bebbeb534e852c03a86799a25072358362a57f74528205d","0d900bdfc02e1ad343baf8825e1994f4f6b4eb7ad73b34be39a004fac23c6932","64b07f53f07ccc2efd1c65df74a9e0cfd942e96bdacf6f43764555baf3a3435b","00774c319a898b4e3b04ac29fde0c786386c1159aeddb82d409050770833ef22","6b36e49d9cb5d2cbd9cfb545cdf774bf9c8462be7d042eeea3a8b6340b249812","f5a05184f4b5e63303f19dfc179ec154e33ebe4760961a2995d5d30d8e9d5ff4","0b2bac41b128534522f33e42d8ef6c5d41ac2435d320241b992660b6e57a5d36","f0d46bb7356ed6e1c5eaf7cfb5abc57800cc75c2a158b6edcaf60aecb02d7015","f5d29b857540383d06250d6aa65ea22e5450a8e151f88d4dc8f8e91c91d47733","f1919e1d8d70ec324d52aa55eaad6b0c9b3812a7eece4a51323d12f4dff656ec","0ea2d18d480489cfae4c48fd0001b319e3c0d4b14748e3c8be538d7be852d32f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The RedCap UE that supports barring exemption for emergency call (see TS 38.306 [24]) and 2Rx branches shall treat this cell as an acceptable cell.","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When cellBarred-eRedCap1Rx is set to \"barred\" and barringExemptEmergencyCall is present in SIB1, if the cell will not be treated as barred by the UE for any reason other than the cellBarred-eRedCap1Rx being set to \"barred\" (see TS 38.331 [3]), and cell selection criteria are fulfilled as defined in clause 5.2.3,","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The eRedCap UE that supports barring exemption for emergency call (see TS 38.306 [24]) and only 1Rx branch shall treat this cell as an acceptable cell.","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When cellBarred-eRedCap2Rx is set to \"barred\" and barringExemptEmergencyCall is present in SIB1, if the cell will not be treated as barred by the UE for any reason other than the cellBarred-eRedCap2Rx being set to \"barred\" (see TS 38.331 [3]), and cell selection criteria are fulfilled as defined in clause 5.2.3,","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The eRedCap UE that supports barring exemption for emergency call (see TS 38.306 [24]) and 2Rx branches shall treat this cell as an acceptable cell.","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When cellBarred2RxXR and barringExemptEmergencyCall are both present in SIB1, if the cell will not be treated as barred by the UE for any reason other than the cellBarred2RxXR being present in SIB1 (see TS 38.331 [3]), and cell selection criteria are fulfilled as defined in clause 5.2.3,","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The 2Rx XR UE that supports barring exemption for emergency call (see TS 38.306 [24]) shall treat this cell as an acceptable cell.","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the cell status is considered as “not barred” according to the above,","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is neither IAB-MT nor NCR-MT;","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When cell status is indicated as “not barred” and “not reserved” for operator use and not “true” for other use and not “true” for future use,","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE shall treat this cell as candidate during the cell selection and cell reselection procedures.","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When cell broadcasts any CAG-IDs or NIDs and the cell status is indicated as \"not barred\" and \"not reserved\" for operator use and \"true\" for other use, and not \"true\" for future use:","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The NPN-capable UE shall treat this cell as candidate during the cell selection and cell reselection procedures","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The non-NPN-capable UE shall treat this cell as if cell status is \"barred\".","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When cell status is indicated as \"true\" for other use, and either cell does not broadcast any CAG-IDs or NIDs or does not broadcast any CAG-IDs and the UE is not operating in SNPN Access Mode,","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE shall treat this cell as if cell status is \"barred\".","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When cell status is indicated as \"true\" for future use,","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE shall treat this cell as if cell status is \"barred\".","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When cell status is indicated as \"not barred\" and \"reserved\" for operator use for any PLMN/SNPN and not \"true\" for other use and not \"true\" for future use,","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-UEs assigned to Access Identity 11 or 15 operating in their HPLMN/EHPLMN shall treat this cell as candidate during the cell selection and reselection procedures if the field cellReservedForOperatorUse for that PLMN set to \"reserved\".","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-UEs assigned to Access Identity 11 or 15 shall treat this cell as candidate during the cell selection and reselection procedures if the field cellReservedForOperatorUse for selected/registered SNPN is set to \"reserved\".","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-UEs assigned to an Access Identity 0, 1, 2 and 12 to 14 shall behave as if the cell status is \"barred\" in case the cell is \"reserved for operator use\" for the registered PLMN/SNPN or the selected PLMN/SNPN.","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-UEs assigned to Access Identity 3 shall behave as if the cell status is \"barred\" in case the cell is \"reserved for operator use\" for the registered PLMN or the selected PLMN.","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:Access Identities 11, 15 are only valid for use in the HPLMN/ EHPLMN and registered/selected SNPN; Access Identities 12, 13, 14 are only valid for use in the home country and registered/selected SNPN as specified in TS 22.261 [12].","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ceb2fed5ac41aa5a70361f6c6857a182e415c356d359a9f953135cf514892f5a","original_member_sha256":"315f0f255b36340f21e8203b9b979c7ecc29e421ee45b443dd903b4e229dd079","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["36e5abc5e0c96f4674c1b189b6dcf984886d3a48bd08154a94b58bf2bfb383ad","7c847fe0fd9f01bf8855514306b81e75735547a52840a2fd3e53171e8fedb3fc","484c20c196ae736f2153ab63af7d1731cbbb5b1d0369af4b493cc9bc4f0fabc7","68fc48f34afa1a2805a0a47014dd04056f31cb1f7768142f4790804ee554711f","cf320423799627f57642180bd7c29fd12a37329e826932ef55a1d4a07ff35639","04f8215ae0a3ff36782f4c4201936b4e72d4a938c4962a7584fe8017020917a3","21639e8c0ab6c4ba0239edce32db6828ba09563c113407afbb4aa4046d88ebd0","e4e629f44c3929b7dea18f18da48878847d4c8a70874303921f626ce8dc47d52","22b83256c5cb496d9e50d6044888f9c5a88e309d590a3dc547469ad651c94b67","8bbeb310efc28a240a843ad15269b1f94f78ba51f252b90870f1377d762f5fcb","0550b9e8380f41bc17a9ac32c0a438ca2fbed4058ae6377328e85cfaa85f2562","1e2e0db7103975a1f146d71c62a46b0e61a5a96d74f855d525b022cb120f59db","7fe252fac6e728fe72779fa7965da8767cd61b87568793884da1a829ef8787e8","b524362684753afa7d12d24482fe629ce8bfc792e83bf983a074df2034dcbbe4","4c70eb7d853a8985eaf4dc0f9102ea4126c60c7ac3ede4078c0016d01ed1bc7c","5083e0e1334485914588f7f89d90bfa40239738bf28a74b8659d37f3e42dc235","7320b1fa8f1917530d58dc3a48fcdf82608639b927696fbdc1e4240ed7724332","396caed754b340798405165be84053996080130ba2961b338ca69d97bac08d2b","a5a0765ce9880eeae4961b5fc38fcc30bbdcdc2387bf5633e3ce266b3b8de343","fbcfccebaef241d7df8353f3c0d33c77e3171ded930a933f2cd1831aab59c276","1727c323ab480b35cb21afca5d9d50c3ec6b77ec644b71082e043db192c69dd3","71b4cfe2d4e90ab6efdc84da18063234fddaf540a46bfa3c3b0e329bcfa22421","ba292c4719846f5e56c93b6f078f75b9530d35760addfa06ff389ea4a967c4c9","d84c6eca588e86888f60178b9d559f99ff778dd7f09f226ad745ba9eb8ba4932"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1a:Access Identity 3 is only valid for PLMNs that indicate to potential Disaster Inbound Roamers that the UEs can access the PLMN as specified in TS 22.261 [12].","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is NPN-capable IAB-MT or NCR-MT;","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When cell broadcasts any CAG-IDs or NIDs and the cell status is indicated as \"not reserved\" for operator use and \"true\" for other use, and not \"true\" for future use:","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE shall treat this cell as candidate during the cell selection and cell reselection procedures.","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When cell status \"barred\" is indicated or to be treated as if the cell status is \"barred\",","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE is not permitted to select/reselect this cell, not even for emergency calls;","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE shall select another cell according to the following rule:","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell is to be treated as if the cell status is \"barred\" due to being unable to acquire the MIB:","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for up to 300 seconds.","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select another cell on the same frequency if the selection criteria are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-else:","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is a RedCap UE, the UE shall acquire SIB1 and, in the remainder of this procedure, consider 'intraFreqReselection in MIB' to be 'intraFreqReselectionRedCap in SIB1', if available; or,","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is an eRedCap UE, the UE shall acquire SIB1 and, in the remainder of this procedure, consider 'intraFreqReselection in MIB' to be 'intraFreqReselection-eRedCap in SIB1', if available; or,","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is a 2Rx XR UE, the UE shall acquire SIB1 and, in the remainder of this procedure, consider 'intraFreqReselection in MIB' to be 'intraFreqReselection2RxXR in SIB1', if available:","paragraph_zero_based":205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell is to be treated as if the cell status is \"barred\" due to being unable to acquire the SIB1:","paragraph_zero_based":206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for up to 300 seconds.","paragraph_zero_based":207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select another cell on the same frequency if the selection criteria are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell status \"barred\" is indicated in MIB but the UE is unable to acquire the SIB1; or","paragraph_zero_based":209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is a RedCap UE and intraFreqReselectionRedCap in SIB1 is not available; or ","paragraph_zero_based":210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is an eRedCap UE and intraFreqReselection-eRedCap in SIB1 is not available; or","paragraph_zero_based":211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is a 2Rx XR UE and intraFreqReselection2RxXR in SIB1 is not available:","paragraph_zero_based":212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE shall exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for 300 seconds.","paragraph_zero_based":213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select another cell on the same frequency if re-selection criteria are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE is neither a RedCap UE nor an eRedCap UE nor a 2Rx XR UE; or,","paragraph_zero_based":215}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ceb2fed5ac41aa5a70361f6c6857a182e415c356d359a9f953135cf514892f5a","original_member_sha256":"315f0f255b36340f21e8203b9b979c7ecc29e421ee45b443dd903b4e229dd079","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["153513e7d8f249439044e546af3e3569530170955063a8953cd3126ec8a75cee","cd9fc5725efea3055dd0825060ef48d35feacbf01f8254c601fc79a444931b45","08bcc19ca2a2156d4123795fa618ad27f878fbe38635f9e9dd70c6150758dd2c","31c41283c0e2fcaf3ddbd02a19ba83fb0c40070c20c3d6edd252f6b30bf976b9","04f6a67bc48abc08e072388183732ea32c1d26573575f6f6eda89b7c71b3d6e6","c67ed5695873881844a63c529804a115f1b9f1fe52f68332023e88029385980b","79d3fe21901134c87a47ec835e8f12aa483ed0c703632407e8be84c6600a9860","856cb44dc494fa9e80fcc01769c883343187d0069aeca5bf52452103b1200cef","959f93c2a7a21cab6645d3056f0e0854d0e531df79cdd5605d1c8ab27a421036","588408bbabfc2cbcf01782099c7a2ead25ff152a46af5e5a1962426cfdb3d819","e486678fc077ea2ad1b2d841e7bcd226f6e2bedaf97dae5450715e1be75c637c","6a3a837d5b1eb87d32dd83cbf4f8f78abba1d98c166839ab62c4ae700182d058","ec206e6ed6f63e2125ab186269f089d4c2eb53e4a9067f79a1c3db5b848375cc","63f9966b762d4d2138d0b87347f6381cd6e63273c82773b8c6e982eff1cf7290","d08bc42a851ff4a2d471d89ccd3aca1eb8c8c5511709d45a3fad420918f0663c","9555b20cda56ff3e4cebed747efaf9affb57977494ae1516d08f78c71be91772","f627b49aa88f976361764d9252d7adc4357a2d2afd5d2c3578258c87f16a4f9c","735f5e82ad57a240fe5715d030d584a422a66edb95dd85c77fc9fd7b82467eaf","2a02ba396638a487b8fe2a6a63ac3de3981928362e067d7160e65279044774c6","d2e164007e86d85fce7a2d54eff4d999f9285e38b52712d3e5b85fe0e91b8eb3","45591c54e9f8da8fa4f5c4d2dd69383c76ab4ceb5f9322ea91b3d7ba4c1cd723","054c0fd36b59a6d6fc392b7338d21293abb4627a2c8f31771983f81dbece3278","f69c4fdcfc76cceb0be00e0d57c159ca6726c5906d408805f262f1f92d14ea84","538e901611e481a8488841fb4a23b8b978a8019fb11d811c812d325f7c21b5f3"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[192,215],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx:p192"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2408370.zip::R2-2408370.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-if the UE is a RedCap UE and intraFreqReselectionRedCap in SIB1 is available; or,","paragraph_zero_based":216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-if the UE is an eRedCap UE and intraFreqReselection-eRedCap in SIB1 is available; or,","paragraph_zero_based":217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-if the UE is a 2Rx XR UE and intraFreqReselection2RxXR in SIB1 is available:","paragraph_zero_based":218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the field intraFreqReselection in MIB message is set to \"allowed\":","paragraph_zero_based":219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select another cell on the same frequency if re-selection criteria are fulfilled;","paragraph_zero_based":220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell is to be treated as if the cell status is \"barred\" due to being unable to acquire the SIB1:","paragraph_zero_based":221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for up to 300 seconds;","paragraph_zero_based":222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-else:","paragraph_zero_based":223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE shall exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for 300 seconds.","paragraph_zero_based":224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the field intraFreqReselection in MIB message is set to \"not allowed\":","paragraph_zero_based":225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell is to be treated as if the cell status is \"barred\" due to being unable to acquire the SIB1:","paragraph_zero_based":226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for up to 300 seconds;","paragraph_zero_based":227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell operates in licensed spectrum:","paragraph_zero_based":228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE shall not re-select to another cell on the same frequency as the barred cell and exclude such cell(s) as candidate(s) for cell selection/reselection for 300 seconds;","paragraph_zero_based":229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-else:","paragraph_zero_based":230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select to another cell on the same frequency if the reselection criteria are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-else:","paragraph_zero_based":232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the cell operates in licensed spectrum, or if this cell belongs to a PLMN which is indicated as being equivalent to the registered PLMN or the selected PLMN of the UE, or if this cell belongs to an SNPN which is equal to or indicated as being equivalent to the registered SNPN or the selected SNPN of the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE shall not re-select to another cell on the same frequency as the barred cell and exclude such cell(s) as candidate(s) for cell selection/reselection for 300 seconds;","paragraph_zero_based":234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-else:","paragraph_zero_based":235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select to another cell on the same frequency if the reselection criteria are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE shall exclude the barred cell as a candidate for cell selection/reselection for 300 seconds.","paragraph_zero_based":237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else if the UE is IAB-MT or NCR-MT:","paragraph_zero_based":238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the UE may select another cell on the same frequency if re-selection criteria are fulfilled;","paragraph_zero_based":239}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ceb2fed5ac41aa5a70361f6c6857a