number is 8;","paragraph_zero_based":117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The mandatory supported PDCP SN length is 12 bits while 18 bits being optional;","paragraph_zero_based":118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The mandatory supported RLC AM SN length is 12 bits while 18 bits being optional;","paragraph_zero_based":119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9f70bee92f76649c6ed81d740db642fdfd93605b3845feafe499297c6a4d2e50","original_member_sha256":"d3bc2fd41c3f8e34d6778be1d149eaa1e928aa6297949f72f4cd287ce304e992","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b5278d174087b168db871947f144233b7f07b7a8b29ea7018d58e7a13f344a25","2d95147d968edc0f783689a03cad07f42838b95699ba4a3000c456940e6564eb","69aee5229429aab3dd05796f68e483643658164a42bd4faecbc53bf432021c89","9bfc0f8d40cb86613d2100851953926861c436adf8520241a4eea253985f369e","b1dc76421c6b6b6c0fa3cb673d5ac8e3bab65e4e4d12297a8d599dca68a5fc8b","632171e15d22b6c510467a1af5b59156868b02c69e75683f8d2e5a11f6cab297","8a0f2b5ddd803779f180c581caddba3f68ca5f0d3306ecab78b9930c06424304","0788b4ba4179b03e1ec7054042c406335a1a700cf276a299fa18522cddc8f96e","2d4008c69504886c3cbabf1d64fdcc66c7e116e7f3ca267a8afe5dba45685ce4","b70cc95f375711ebc8280a7263ebba45c287f807eee540373a34a17efbefd71d","0c1296db4ad7d6c2e0900cceee89d37b565cddda1b9c7b1d14f196b31de8ab7a","d24b4ebeb0308c1cede5583fde0078732fd788672cd70c38bed8727a64b6670b","e55fddcefb770b7e9f4426c15ea68db2e76e0e3cb070e56a840fa12148d8a0b1","2432d6295678a7e5304edf9774d4724e4886f0903d4fb2b62e126df27089f5a8","a1a099f121c3757fe31e92b0b6335c50c5f82760be67a4b1958c504816a6e40d","169c3f36d51986b483e26b37a0030e1faf10b7411694b4770e1024dca4abfb7b","bee1be91d3c04d7ab31c47d01e09f9ae47040e445448ef82f3a37666e0d5b05a","d02e8cbd697ae1810074c3012247d88e70339f7889a7482c352e21eca4a8f878","33e5d435de38e7fe3ba804ecc178ee85ae874bb55f5b843ab81f09527d701e41","565ddaad95f8e15c77b3d1405db264d2b121b8203b73a8ddd814c525044842c5","594149ca44921d5a82b23a2b8f6e0fbf749c652665ae0d3e07c296b0f7bc0109","0fbfaeb3e66d9edc98a3dc3a52d4de37fd23b51b4118be68b72aff0294997ef3","61cbcf85a67f2d173c01ba5ed9ebcda960c7e3d072e19040a799eb3b34832816","0440db5594303a5662a5bf848db7fa47b154b23c83ed3ee659c2ef91a4629d39"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2409923.zip::R2-2409923 Clarification on LTM capabilities.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2409923.zip::R2-2409923 Clarification on LTM capabilities.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For FR1, 1 DL MIMO layer if 1 Rx branch is supported, and 2 DL MIMO layers if 2 Rx branches are supported; for FR2, either 1 or 2 DL MIMO layers can be supported, while 2 Rx branches are always supported. For FR1 and FR2, UE features and corresponding capabilities related to more than 2 UE Rx branches or more than 2 DL MIMO layers, as well as UE features and capabilities related to more than 1 UE Tx branch or more than 1 UL MIMO layer are not supported by RedCap UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-CA, MR-DC, DAPS, CPAC, LTM SCG, IAB (i.e., the RedCap UE is not expected to act as IAB node), and NCR (i.e., the RedCap UE is not expected to act as NCR-MT) related UE features and corresponding capabilities are not supported by RedCap UEs. All other feature groups or components of the feature groups as captured in TR 38.822 [24] as well as capabilities specified in this specification remain applicable for RedCap UEs same as other UEs, unless indicated otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2.22.1Definition of eRedCap UE","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eRedCap UE is the UE with reduced peak data rate and, with or without reduced baseband bandwidth in FR1:","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The maximum bandwidth is 20 MHz for FR1. UE features and corresponding capabilities related to UE bandwidths wider than 20 MHz in FR1 are not supported by eRedCap UEs. eRedCap UEs do not support operation in FR2 and in FR1 60kHz SCS.","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-CA, MR-DC, DAPS, CPAC, LTM SCG, IAB (i.e., the eRedCap UE is not expected to act as IAB node), and NCR (i.e., the eRedCap UE is not expected to act as NCR-MT) related UE features and corresponding capabilities are not supported by eRedCap UEs. All other feature groups or components of the feature groups as captured in TR 38.822 [24] as well as capabilities specified in this specification remain applicable for eRedCap UEs same as other UEs, unless indicated otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":126}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9f70bee92f76649c6ed81d740db642fdfd93605b3845feafe499297c6a4d2e50","original_member_sha256":"d3bc2fd41c3f8e34d6778be1d149eaa1e928aa6297949f72f4cd287ce304e992","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["208d428cf5d71928e9d43cd18db61f7fd3d5daa89f25b56b9d8115257b37eb7c","f5a8bdf8077c312b9e0ff3e3981a168a037e4ccd65cc6e6448b417cc7e5fee15","433f49456d20939c129b84a4abe4e5f73d04d57f32bbd87385ed5b39b9f00b40","ba413df780abe572f7fe3de50ccd8a2d8d83bb6d370e1990dd0e517d22014262","0444238ef6da729e3609af2cb70350a3ab7789807f0f7079078f009a09df9c36","66b5b3eaa13b5880941c7d9d956d4be78e6683f9cf736915e0b48bb2e7973e8a","c9ceea77872410f7e1683d3d2b20268f57ede366559f8682b57ba93714dd52ba"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,126],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2409923.zip::R2-2409923 Clarification on LTM capabilities.docx:p120"}
