ody and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fd48c45b72d5de350f978eaabe5a946734047360cd6be645acac95ab7aa9b5aa","original_member_sha256":"ae901254ac2c48e23dcd25b500bb364317eea716dac35cf5aadf7e644acfc16d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8d38fb0e860ac143628b248f1e01ea1035e5ca8585b26fbd7745d76a7ca0b65a","9412b9bbb89f7d8f10a1bca58dfe456846ff194b642277f70dede8f7b31bb444","35bd02902d389b71aaf0e0d948462f57a37f7f73b57e7921f177a316e634e5ac","5dd248348ffa471a16099a84e62f793887205007b86a92473ea8a5be3cca2ab5","002968a83b98971e76eedc4e85f578962da738fa0fcf4bda3dbee15f448ee445","522f661fe07ca8180ae36e13f96c02d38f52608f6185596c937a23ae5faee7e6","905d1203c1ce051d456d7d9aab3ef45a2933ff952e60198964b7666b80be9e2d","afe109882ed26783c31802dc01b574852424a85899c74b14ff4639d33a9b24fc","21bd98b6ffeb3d1766acacfd36df20f18d4fb3dc199209b4a89e4fdd1da76686","a39bda012f64d7f8f7a09f28dbf4693bb1e50dde3fe9c0c8b337c3bfc838de1d","ff2df6f9f05e6f83472889e1751779a9d3fc5b9ed6e926f2d3b0b31bbb59e824","39baf184f8705ff900a2c8f5f21dec2596ad2ed1a31f594884d6c691977584b2","7db18ee2c08fec356e1fffc3249fd5017e9128a630bc766243756558ea379e29","d88c8f600d370cf0d67b7c322415c8b1fb0bfa2aca84fef6abda0b6d769af469","845d324768a0982442a8327f2c782098b791b83f248b7e8348614dcf7ea81adb","8aca9571b64b7f44aff734b16cf8a47eb9c6f8df615f3d1a7f6d8142daf08a8c","984c147b2e2a5b1616fece0549796590e3617056ad1c2814d190781dae43bcb1","274b517012eb23271f1058074a34477a6d75d2adac367552ce1e1caf4373dbb3","723ebf758d65e5ae0c52b7e7e1bb84f0104c76bacead1bd48612c2cffd8dd860","c4c3252a2204746d14cf8e36dd812ae4a213dae3e2b82990e6be71fb6e40528e","a656fce614824616caf73010e82a681d4c0c352d831b7c3570418544c4159069","e72114f5a4834e3f084a72b6a6aebd4e6093ce575aca1ba45631c70f985e1cce","b3a486a1f6f141075ce2d414c9b974272cd6668e1815955b06f4b6a3af7b5df1","8359efc7d2b5dda9af5ac068b92bdd5d51fae5fba7947438a8eae2439f358a76"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[24,47],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx:p24"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19) Rel-20(Release 20)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In R16, we have introduced on-demand SIB request in RRC_CONNECTED by dedicated and SIB delivery by RRC message RRCReconfiguration. The lists of SIB and posSIBs that are supported in the RRCReconfiguration message are as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For different releases, segmentation of SIB/posSIB is supported. For SIB, segmentation is supported in the RRC layer for SIB12, SIB17, SIB17bis, SIB23; for posSIB, segmentation is supported in the LPP layer for all the posSIBs. ","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"With the above two features, we need to consider how SIB/posSIB segments can be sent by dedicated RRC signalling in RRC_CONNECTED. First, for SIB, if the network wants to deliver the requested SIB in RRCReconfiguration, they can be sent without segmentation since the maximum PDCP size can be as large as 9000 byte","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next, for posSIBs, similar to normal SIBs, multiple segments of the same posSIB can be delivered by different items of SIBs within the SI message. Then, within the LPP spec, the meta-data is defined, according to which the posSIB can be re-assembled. The reason why it cannot be done as normal SIB is because the posSIB are not generated by the gNB but by the LMF and the content of the posSIB is transparent to the gNB. ","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Then problem with the current spec is that there is the restriction that two segments cannot be included in the same SI message. This is reasonable for SI message delivery by broadcast since it does not make sent to segment SIB if they are included in the same SI message. But this does not make sense if we want to support delivery of different posSIB segments by dedicated signaling. The reason is that the LMF is responsible for the segmentation of the posSIBs and the gNB just transparently forwards the posSIB (segments). ","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fd48c45b72d5de350f978eaabe5a946734047360cd6be645acac95ab7aa9b5aa","original_member_sha256":"ae901254ac2c48e23dcd25b500bb364317eea716dac35cf5aadf7e644acfc16d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c0826f9fa5d4631eefc69ffd5c0c762fcd3a1f44bc65988d57371f305e0c368c","0507536c4e7a3e0a7609f915ced4494f95569655e2f1aa28f09ac910fa04bc76","2d8ee4f749ea340ef829859626a43700455346b9a5f90f6a878ac443559011d5","017e8c6346c26fcc1c8e3ad40dd3a8f1b4717634ee16aa143842fbe0a0677416","1f287fc9deb2348d929f6d2f3cf1dcf597de01f956d6f5e7dccc37b565e18ac9","3123abe3e28e24279929b203e902e53f7846616d4db290f8ea422c74907cf0fb","de2f31627847a6c0895afa850ab0b1dc23b35569c5c9f10c59b8f4845cb2bbe2","fd7f45dfcc13e8442c0d9e5818e50027a88119e276703ca563fa96eb220f9b58","dcde7e24adca29e395fd142b0a416ddcd8f4e1667db2025a7d4fe515498290b4","875390017a3241be4cfbc8771fb75181351faccb521bfcad719c34e970bcb18c","62a69a869a8490f9ee735cc34809a1677f54387ff98f330a431353213fcfff5f","30ac0b8c338ad5a1a62aa410e6ee6cfdea260d495dd1a9150f07568ef322a8f4","d5b8f7bdc722dcc7426718017e7065380bf88722b63539d00b085d9e9454649b","543d0d0c1b150ecc878b71e849e90a00dbea31c97515256ca4dd80f7c48455e2","5b995b9cf1d628954780c0e0507d5fe7e43ddcccefbf466f83cb8e3b7024dba8","7ecef98337213edc1a024d458dbc73f1cae11b4048d11196995610352739d239","3d19029747ae28a9e332933f178727e61bb460be7882ff722dcf97f7ae637069","bc81948b2f9e30f16606133dbad8f1b11825ad996e4006eb768e8d57fc52ea89","8e783e876a68503ef4a65fee9dfcbedc0b1aca2686c37c1b7f3d37ac6a865403","df1472a5030619c82004ff2532947bf096184fb482e68850ea4c946c5d7d8249","f7ea502273ba17e48622c03ed8ea49849fb66c62b019925091cbd0cff1c0b7c7","5b37055f62977d4ec94d998d4accb0426708305ec5738e399ee422123e9e06d7","ae19f3e941fd95d98f6a8de8ba736e335715bc749fbd598ebeed8dcdc2d884de","3ca1005f9787087da2d93574c1d5cfd3cbb9d324b4bc3341fd002f482510f665"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[48,71],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx:p48"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"One might argue that the posSIB can be sent by multiple instances of RRCReconfig message periodically like the current posSIB/SIB by broadcast. This might work for cases when the UE is in good coverage and in low mobility scenairo. But for high mobility scenario where the posSIB is time-sensitive and bad coverage scenairo when the TB size is small, this is not possible. Also, delivery of multiple RRC reconfig message is quite in-efficient.","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Based on the discussion above, we think that it is necessary to remove the restriction in the RRC spec for dedicated signaling","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Remove the restriction that different segments of the posSIBs in the same SI message if the SI message is delivered by the dedicated signaling.","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted functionality:","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"posSIB request in RRC_CONNECTED","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted 5G architecture options:","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR SA","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-operability:","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may unexpectedly receive multiple instances of the same posSIB types within a single SI message when delivered by dedicated signalling, which is currently not allowed by the spec","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the UE is implemented according to the CR while the NW is not, there is no inter-operability issue","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"It remains unclear how segmented posSIBs can be delivered via dedicated signalling”","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Clauses affected:","paragraph_zero_based":94},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.1, 6.2.2","paragraph_zero_based":95}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fd48c45b72d5de350f978eaabe5a946734047360cd6be645acac95ab7aa9b5aa","original_member_sha256":"ae901254ac2c48e23dcd25b500bb364317eea716dac35cf5aadf7e644acfc16d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["3f80edea9bf4e09574885c1fd326b2ce906e47f3eebff01b82357759e78f1ba9","3ef08b1bf5523f4c575fbf11a24bfe2e96bdead34a4ae01fa4cba1cacca3b05b","788d507f16b6175f9b6748f4d74a9792776dd3b6ffd551cb85f920002c05870f","b6447942d6417987fc54f082864c26af8abac4a7c1642c712eb6a704c8999931","385692d94f1efb783ea0dec9208105d37dd1ec140329e5aa2abc379fad4b7198","e3666410386a04155a7fec2922b9b7371c275b27b5d336bbbfcffb89faf9a688","db230b8e669e6ec52df4bf6b4f1f6c3b5d9feb416fb17a4ba351738c04eb1a4b","065e4fc0fb0014f8c507844a904fd7b92b72caae513e1a2d7f23cbaf12e160b4","8baeb4c228986f926014d6d10b0aee32022f7e