s"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fd48c45b72d5de350f978eaabe5a946734047360cd6be645acac95ab7aa9b5aa","original_member_sha256":"ae901254ac2c48e23dcd25b500bb364317eea716dac35cf5aadf7e644acfc16d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["784679b9ece48bc118ea916967a28f1b929640f09786858ac3fb1d27461c6786","3d1c7328adf542f5a17697d287ebd1df9e2e06d6940ce5adf0350e6453b80db7","48ad010af36bdd1b202355083d2caeeef87efa366ede29528adb48afb15f546d","3c61759023005d37005cf90e1e2aac3a806f54599735de539d39101535a5b90d","96c41515b9a327f2816e14e41ea123794df0f1567f96c2c5735e1076c19c1d48","3396d5a792dcb11c0ceca991dc28f7edebe9b1659851c004c69b0df7a62565ae","dacee1da741984859cd2767a2c4ef49ddcf79236166848a96cd56f8ffea86e66","d9c4d475f32039bf45f68bd49ee2590c7bb555dbc60784cf340a5d268472af22","6e75e1f5579b95ea1c1755913b5038bee097a38e5a247bedb55c3ecb4dfe86ff","66dbc9111b60ac7b98c1819c59c83fd3b2c2125c9cc191e3e615ba2f992411eb","a8e3def95abbeae78b24940e013f10c8930c9e59ea878b448214531978090353","2dd917382c89ff95e7ecc00d7ab19c091aa406fe8e15becb7939b0944593a556","7bb8190d03c5dee4a795582fa5bec2c025ce7e65b672bed8fa2ad8553111a48d","2831b871169459344acbbfb5b2e1305a79bfcdc75aefeb52bc3561f94fc01588","75ab2af0056048dfa4cc0813e6898b997b31904166b8c0841265f4ac0783c961","7f226640b5836af0cd94d526bb2f72dc76e1c1ffb2eaf7596caa08dfd6c41f1b","959a9337e143faa5187df866922f7bcc43c0328c795a3d6aaa4a283019d6495f","dbeebee85c12af34d4ca787672407fdfa9dbcc9f1605e936e461de47e3fd3c14","ae680d36ab18604010eb60dfd513e76c7ca48cb8bbf9968bccdc214ecee42981","2c21da29a88e1b42ff6ba6e31acbc8cc5363d553d46551f5affc79ef6ec1cadf","d7b7fa641ca4599b5ca3b0c425ff76c4527e32b7d9da8461b9005c6c4df2b323","d757cf08db5000810588a4cc9001fb40783bb4ea58c50c44e679483ff0d071be","a62fe4746453883b2d86638667e6f31da6e95c961e1c96d9d43f5f60405e0713","259990e7aefa7e32ab38712860c56993adcbb88b048ee596ae0c98cfe9beb3f7"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Other comments:","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR's revision history:","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"================================FIRST CHANGE=====================================","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5Procedures","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2System information","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"System Information (SI) is divided into the MIB and a number of SIBs and posSIBs where:","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the MIB is always transmitted on the BCH with a periodicity of 80 ms and repetitions made within 80 ms (TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.1) and it includes parameters that are needed to acquire SIB1 from the cell. The first transmission of the MIB is scheduled in subframes as defined in TS 38.213 [13], clause 4.1 and repetitions are scheduled according to the period of SSB;","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:If the period of SSB is larger than 80 ms, the MIB is transmitted with the same periodicity as that of SSB.","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the SIB1 is transmitted on the DL-SCH with a periodicity of 160 ms and variable transmission repetition periodicity within 160 ms as specified in TS 38.213 [13], clause 13. The default transmission repetition periodicity of SIB1 is 20 ms but the actual transmission repetition periodicity is up to network implementation. For SSB and CORESET multiplexing pattern 1, SIB1 repetition transmission period is 20 ms. For SSB and CORESET multiplexing pattern 2/3, SIB1 transmission repetition period is the same as the SSB period (TS 38.213 [13], clause 13). SIB1 includes information regarding the availability and scheduling (e.g. mapping of SIBs to SI message, periodicity, SI-window size) of other SIBs with an indication whether one or more SIBs are only provided on-demand and, in that case, the configuration needed by the UE to perform the SI request. SIB1 is cell-specific SIB;","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SIBs other than SIB1 and posSIBs are carried in SystemInformation (SI) messages, which are transmitted on the DL-SCH. Only SIBs or posSIBs having the same periodicity can be mapped to the same SI message. SIBs and posSIBs are mapped to different SI messages, i.e. an SI message contains either only SIBs or only posSIBs. Each SI message is transmitted within periodically occurring time domain windows (referred to as SI-windows with same length for all SI messages). Each SI message is associated with an SI-window and the SI-windows of different SI messages do not overlap. That is, within one SI-window only the corresponding SI message is transmitted. An SI message may be repeated with the same content a number of times within the SI-window. Any SIB or posSIB except SIB1 can be configured to be cell specific or area specific, using an indication in SIB1. The cell specific SIB is applicable only within a cell that provides the SIB while the area specific SIB is applicable within an area referred to as SI area, which consists of one or several cells and is identified by systemInformationAreaID;","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The mapping of SIBs to SI messages is configured in schedulingInfoList and schedulingInfoList2, while the mapping of posSIBs to SI messages is configured in posSchedulingInfoList and schedulingInfoList2.Each SIB and each posSIB is mapped to a single SI message. posSIBs of the same posSibType carrying GNSS Generic Assistance Data for different GNSS/SBAS (identified by gnss-id/sbas-id, see TS 37.355 [49]) are mapped to different SI messages.Each SIBis contained at most once in an SI message. Each posSIB is contained at most once in an SI message when delivered by broadcast signalling.For SIBs and posSIBs with segments when delivered by broadcast signalling, the segments contained in SI messages are transmitted according to the SI message periodicity, with one segment of a particular sibType/posSibType in each SI message;","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For a UE in RRC_CONNECTED, the network can provide system information through dedicated signalling using the RRCReconfiguration message, e.g. if the UE has an active BWP with no common search space configured to monitor system information, paging, or upon request from the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For PSCell and SCells, the network provides the required SI by dedicated signalling, i.e. within an RRCReconfiguration message. Nevertheless, the UE shall acquire MIB of the PSCell to get SFN timing of the SCG (which may be different from MCG). Upon change of relevant SI for SCell, the network releases and adds the concerned SCell. For PSCell, the required SI can only be changed with Reconfiguration with Sync.","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The physical layer imposes a limit to the maximum size a SIB can take. The maximum SIB1 or SI message size is 2976 bits.","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"=============================================NEXT CHANGE==============================================================","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6Protocol data units, formats and parameters (ASN.1)","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.2RRC messages","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fd48c45b72d5de350f978eaabe5a946734047360cd6be645acac95ab7aa9b5aa","original_member_sha256":"ae901254ac2c48e23dcd25b500bb364317eea716dac35cf5aadf7e644acfc16d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["63625534dabc7296e677e59ee24321c36ff62a07d465ca4598654a3fd164621f","a6fd359b5ba3c2ec9782a045539f692ee58e50bdba5a64baee99c7e9930a5083","24e4c5a2500614681df434381d1530d43d419c915a3aad3ff44b0ab825362b5a","eb2d068435b2d1f4e290aad3d11884d19d36ee1b550bbc40639ddcebc0b49b48","cf43b72c8bd241370eed4844c2d5e1be3ce54250c79f79a46b046d349b9872c3","628779527e2a85fc82a2290302f4712897607cfd79d157dc1d114d081eda883f","f0507df9fb21cbb52436ba82fc2184a274eb621c981512e21e5b916c2a080912","e244fdb5a239f65f44adca389016a2d073a1e5413311d0d4dc6c6a4849880631","455e67f106903308875468c66b492f5092a3373503932f9284cf74645d7e0fb3","d9442f2ff7c2ae56c69273dd231e44be0326cde05cbc8f1b36a5aeaf1fb2f99f","172d3c67e7815d8d6bf6f6c62b5ca67225eb020e769548d4e25b54a1501ad04e","97ecec26fb92e054a2fd7b56cb39089bf42234adfe46efeb82fa9319f30221f6","a66e48e8621dddb53a1ec45b8b5e3224510597ed58d937a4f65b3de785065fc3","48f54ea29430ab2fa7567c46a64be44ec35f0607de57c9bf33083dda07c8ced8","a19818e6ea3b847a32a8ac9d1196971f9123f10681b204055c612b1a273d1207","bf8c8de431e0294ac7bffc735ad696b73c002dbc36990dfc79222e25f85d5775","31ce67c6bd3dc1d20ec5f0d9b5d9b7b425b6d470a673a1da8e86d6ac6b43ba22","d9610d3703f787a602dbbbb1345ca2a2e370d903ec4a94e0441599b483d2d9cc","e2df306748261aba75bdcc288daead40fcff1b09493b16edba32bc0bf371c7b0","02ee18e6c883fb355bdcc1c6c52d3a616464da6d0ef5852cb7010bac5b187862","8de62fe8ce10e75052210788f846b01975785c5f1822205cf8017f38f591d1a4","2cd795780c33362f1750d39e1e90722915d6e4736fa91877e9fc70d5eabd855b","98ca8ec5d3b75639b2b4533c32e3c8c7d794bd195637a62956d48ed82872e771","59328173fbf846e3b6e3ad362a9c77d6b0b024b8465357b0cbc5ce2e7e2a24d6"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505640.zip::R2-2505640 Correction on delivery of posSIB segments by dedicated siganling in RRC_CONNECTED_r18.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.2.2Message definitions","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RRCReconfiguration","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The RRCReconfiguration message is the command to modify an RRC connection. It may convey information for measurement configuration, mobility control, radio resource configuration (including RBs, MAC main configuration and physical channel configuration) and AS security configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Signalling radio bearer: SRB1 or SRB3","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RLC-SAP: AM","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Logical channel: DCCH","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Direction: Network to UE","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RRCReconfiguration message","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RRCRECONFIGURATION-START","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RRCReconfiguration ::=                  SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    rrc-TransactionIdentifier               RRC-TransactionIdentifier,","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    criticalExtensions                      CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        rrcReconfiguration                      RRCReconfiguration-IEs,","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        criticalExtensionsFuture                SEQUENCE {}","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RRCReconfiguration-IEs ::=              SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    radioBearerConfig                       RadioBearerConfig                                                      OPTIONAL, -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    secondaryCellGroup                      OCTET STRING (CONTAINING CellGroupConfig)                              OPTIONAL, -- Cond SCG","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    measConfig                              MeasConfig                                                             OPTIONAL, -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    lateNonCriticalExtension                OCTET STRING (CONTAINING RRCReconfiguration-v15t0-IEs)                 OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fd48c45b72d5de350f978eaabe5a946734047360cd6be645acac95ab7aa9b5aa","original_member_sha256":"ae901254ac2c48e23dcd25b500bb364317eea716dac35cf5aadf7e644acfc16d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["bf22157e2c60d645aaf33950227b0d70a29a31af1f29ea22b9a82206c66f860d","65426a62ee938ef456836ec40917bd76eb11ff16157a1f5f4eb58bc232dd1d0a","fb11f4a8c3107fcc3a0871ac3c2313df9278f1002c03952103cc173cd602de19","f3d3e0a7cf350f2451b99918c3f20ad4f65613a02a236302fb28fa9ff72f6f1b","05828f058af7d8f55d6b145c215771b0504eac844435c80cf0e093e1642999ec","c8519cfe0614db7ab3b4a6b4c3c1bd277a5c0b2037e25308427639660b9861ff","ab9612e8c858e395525ec2a9033133234dac7e7af5c7bf01abec1322fc7ad60a","a7f866639c9bc363cebe842e38f171c3d1d8aac265f6f76c05dbff3b6