{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-19","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19) Rel-20(Release 20)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-19 introduces multi-hop L2 U2N relay. RAN2 agreed to use NotificationMessageSidelink when AS-layer issues trigger upstream relay (re)selection, with legacy causes and idle/inactive handling left to upper layers; this avoids inventing a new message or enumerant.","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"At the same time, the 38.351 running CR anchors egress link/channel determination on RRC-configured mappings keyed by (UE ID, BEARER ID) and still carries FFS on the configuration model for indirectly-connected UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR provides a pre-configured egress candidate list per (LocalIdentity, RB) so an intermediate/last relay can locally switch to a backup next hop on AS-layer failure—with no new on-air header—while remaining consistent with service-continuity flows in 38.300. Degradation-based triggers are FFS; this version specifies failure-only triggers. This procedure does not alter key or PDCP contexts; upper layers remain authoritative.","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A new sl-FastFailoverConfig to SL-L2RelayUE-Config, containing a priority-ordered list of egress candidates keyed by (sl-LocalIdentity, RB). Each candidate specifies exactly one interface via a CHOICE {PC5 | Uu}. No new enumerants are introduced for NotificationMessageSidelink.","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Specify relay behavior: upon AS‑layer link failure on the current egress (PC5 RLF/release or Uu RLF/release depending on hop), the relay selects the next available egress candidate by priority without requiring new RRC; then, if the selected change impacts the child, the relay uses NotificationMessageSidelink as already agreed in R2. (No change to the message itself.)","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"424eb093f767dd650e5338895960519d92ebea981f57d2d92b779f748b231a17","original_member_sha256":"c43941f5cb11f87748367ce8365b9a3c5ac1bf79a9c30e779a91aa0d1036aaf3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e4ea5591218aa96d0cd407936b651eb165fb4c75e229dab64ec9de6be991cb96","2d00e3b1a82065155328ddd802c3d4a8ebff11f4a0d6da9ecf9b1e34dc8ebfc8","d3c67396ad1d561f5d31b1789bd89e75f53a154f4818863b6dae8c72b6bb984a","761fa4d36b282591b5f5bb5ee554c6086f6eb9d5925f257d405f142f9e3a17e1","9ee3a8ef1b4d8b5d23ae68c79878f83d9a7ffdf02ec93cff53f7b1de6029f4d6","10ad76c0b37e03f706e2ee885b21328bb46d66115eac9ee2f8c7daa47e95a00c","b08252b53f111fda758564f01d6aeb287a86ceee9730eba0ca5fcf7c7dadb00e","5397ebe3cc2afa3393b897343a62f60e5b485315d8236802a715ec930f5cc336","275fd5f28330e81a71bc0f424bdb9e870b94721e1fbac96c6b96ce5232317404","751ec11cbe1bc9ff3f64bd3ab3359ff43219156cea5f7196169e0f5e258b83f1","16c8d70f7d429c511b56c375317337c5d5c75b5a185ec91bf088b77069963fb7","acd6206245de4b9556a4853ff1b8b41875944834aa76df6c7d72af763f365262","3c4c80e1e11044a4d07c2d065ab1badcf74a3b84af6435503a27154aade28f9b","aa023a0b0d2660ef6c32ba3dcd24e93f4c68368e6cd63681e0271ae11dd37845","9a8d9b329e61c894ddf8760a630191ea73ef62382d1a01e3c6d337a7ce528215","678faa6488dfc3c2c5a12f9ac934c801662cd0b169d122908b487d446c289971","8b24573e0133d1c5ee95e1377545628b16380b4d3d980bde5296376e8173041e","7423559940944ed0cc1fe176b76253cf9035dcdbfc0fac2f3e385feb311a2329","288cc60197c635a28716a1c3a9133085106b36b1009fb0a2849670c1b99dfd9f","532f23fdc4d93473b95460495e72e75b93ed504ad8f2cd192ec3839063fc9f50","1125148dc63048ae715de96f708b7b565110b35212ef0163fd48eecef6b8af5f","23da18bbbcbc650fad7a07ef8006251a7a06ae59113986d1a2b8d37f6d71a8d1","85f9fe225bf206da5b28016fbb39c62cb1368eb1244f4f20547ea6629294dc69","378adf0aa423995360841de5b3ff121413a3320bd55a44c2044b1a4823324310"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[48,71],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx:p48"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Local fast failover in multi‑hop relies on full RRC reconfiguration during failures, increasing interruption time and complexity in scenarios A/B service continuity.","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Clauses affected:","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.15.2; 5.3.5.15.3; 5.3.5.15.3a (new); 5.8.9.10.4; 6.3.5","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Y","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"N","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Other specs","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"X","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":" Other core specifications","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"affected:","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"X","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":" Test specifications","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS/TR ... CR ... ","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"(show related CRs)","paragraph_zero_based":94