{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"X","paragraph_zero_based":96},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":" O&M Specifications","paragraph_zero_based":97},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS/TR ... CR ... ","paragraph_zero_based":98},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":99},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":100},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Other comments:","paragraph_zero_based":101},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":102},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":103},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":104},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR's revision history:","paragraph_zero_based":105},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":106},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":107},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":108},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"START OF CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":109},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.15L2 U2N or U2U Relay UE configuration","paragraph_zero_based":110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.15.1General","paragraph_zero_based":111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The network configures the L2 U2N or U2U Relay UE with relay operation related configurations. For each connected L2 U2N or U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-L2IdentityRemote, the network provides the configuration parameters used for relaying.","paragraph_zero_based":112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if sl-L2RelayUE-Config is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-L2RelayUE-Config contains the sl-RemoteUE-ToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the L2 U2N Remote UE release as specified in 5.3.5.15.2;","paragraph_zero_based":116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-L2RelayUE-Config contains the sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the L2 U2N Remote UE addition/modification as specified in 5.3.5.15.3;","paragraph_zero_based":118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if sl-L2RelayUE-Config is set to release:","paragraph_zero_based":119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"424eb093f767dd650e5338895960519d92ebea981f57d2d92b779f748b231a17","original_member_sha256":"c43941f5cb11f87748367ce8365b9a3c5ac1bf79a9c30e779a91aa0d1036aaf3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a3acef282837b7c37810ff7bc5aec8615686f765172bf3943d4df7cfa6e0e1d7","824e21c4f5a6059ea45ac8c72d86e5676202d6c1e8b859633c11bdc82e6245be","3451bdfd6b31a1ef2b14675aa5ec1b5edfb10f674d5816c290c702097c934565","dc22fc3fc694a1cfefafde03d21c174d4e0c7fcf17bab106e9e00c190e01ebfe","4fb36aa225104e0001ea7bc50f8cdcec8018a31ef024fb1c040bb8ba259960dc","6441cdf01cecf8b62a31b2699a7e53e36e1ee202efb0ce51388d91f5d109ab25","55400acff403ab9102de313252babc44d55c66aec7e85c2860bc33225fe4bcc8","2c4544d273b51904290d2876922aea214e979e30d9441535ff31f6d0f1079c86","38f9888f9404c0f4aa0e0000d0f08d06dd742c114f41a514a480c392b644c39e","c64ec51e0b918344a84e8bd1c12c74557a2162cc714d32298cc28b6618e366e0","8915c3c0f1ffa83b2bad76ba9d594336c82e262d5a00cb759cdabb841a8e9953","d02e8cbd697ae1810074c3012247d88e70339f7889a7482c352e21eca4a8f878","5ae7418cbb80a6b0d50cc42942c7ed1149455d9771e9dcfa71a466e6ea61d9b1","826c33d48c4951c44b42a7f5d7664d9a8a931a25b4c7ecad070ea61074e1b6fe","f08e218293b0ef7709b57f8f6c84eb597cc44efac877bfb4653df0a1c8187c2e","edf5b2ea87884f4df22d305e72215b30014b3bd852c75993fb5e22ce29ae585b","abf0b49d27556d0c7a000f1fd760c7a81122e6577aa93f99f2c8324cefd05afe","72e737d71cf5b014a49630ba6fd6aa30ea7f909b5f2fd3630970dc3c0ff45236","63cd54834f7d57aa60d6a86201cbff1dabba122d2d284eff883ce503cf95e002","a9bd9647a08df9dae27c41c0e6dafbb6912ef39448cb8afe7fd3715f5a26527d","6e6f36399dfb28ffbf01e662c978e49834e1add47f63141b3fde37f0f10ae1dc","73aa96886bd6fa17c86d40344a083285de405bbd0ec5653c881fb97df0dfc992","dcbab0f53057c33764cce18452b84791f3c101273437305244eda468ca916f31","11d0e4489ef352852c2d516f73e0b745f28592f057798d995ca2956ecfa68c17"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the L2 U2N relay operation related configurations.","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2U Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if sl-L2RelayUE-Config is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-L2RelayUE-Config contains the sl-U2U-RemoteUE-ToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the L2 U2U Remote UE release as specified in 5.3.5.15.2;","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-L2RelayUE-Config contains the sl-U2U-RemoteUE-ToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the L2 U2U Remote UE addition/modification as specified in 5.3.5.15.3;","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if sl-L2RelayUE-Config is set to release:","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the L2 U2U relay operation related configurations.","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.15.2L2 U2N or U2U Remote UE Release","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the release is triggered by reception of the sl-RemoteUE-ToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each SL-DestinationIdentity value included in the sl-RemoteUE-ToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the current UE has a PC5 RRC connection to a L2 U2N Remote UE with SL-DestinationIdentity:","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>indicate upper layers to trigger PC5 unicast link release.","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2U Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the release is triggered by reception of the sl-U2U-RemoteUE-ToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each SL-DestinationIdentity value included in the sl-U2U-RemoteUE-ToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the current UE has a PC5-RRC connection to a L2 U2U Remote UE with this SL-DestinationIdentity:","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>release the configuration associated with the L2 U2U Remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Fast failover interaction:","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1> If the release is triggered due to AS-layer failure of an upstream egress link and sl-FastFailoverConfig is configured for the affected sl-L2IdentityRemote,","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2> the relay UE may perform local egress re-selection in accordance with 5.3.5.15.3a.","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> If the re-selection impacts the child UE (e.g., parent change), the relay shall indicate the change to the child using NotificationMessageSidelink as specified in 5.8.9.10.4.","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"424eb093f767dd650e5338895960519d92ebea981f57d2d92b779f748b231a17","original_member_sha256":"c43941f5cb11f87748367ce8365b9a3c5ac1bf79a9c30e779a91aa0d1036aaf3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["158dc55f874cc714e7440f8fed1e4714148048ba93237bb52809ba24d1cd63a5","2219b5f71320fbbb0ea963383a6aada60299cc32bcef350eb65a2d43f358961e","b0b20d526353c230e7f4d310c674e42c444d0d8c6297f22613d1b2dfe9ac9788","db4f3f98a0830cd7401ecd3465f3e6996c2ab68eecd7f1279eb885518188be23","f457405db5f2c4eb71dbcd7a0ff4551ed8e04e4de6861cfacd0bf2f8e25df057","2554ea22a17f81e5410bf840505912abaf6f0d3ed168552527361dcfa0f63338","317a8744de45674d3e7fcdea8fab525f011843be12c83c55237ad7151c5347f5","e68b8011ea083243a7a99e8a92ac8d453a833478623997568fd80fec5efc2f85","04a9f01ad193b4d0fee02a01b5b9b7e4375b3e5cb688c8e847207b900fa78ed5","d19c15b768e3dbd05cb3d0497aff080151944ebd420264f144a90e368e16848c","3e175da0620917e539794b2c840f005259d818f7e65155f9cf971f261933856c","d5044abd4803118718e0ccc56c80ed5489c647a072362d1d73545e7f92da4cf4","19c10b4887524d9e7730086b51fe53b8e2319533d04605fa4755f3eb998f4ab1","0644f85b69f15439183bada35197d110b2ab671fd239da4d0ab2556d53e231af","e1876eab8781c77c15acfdb38fbab910636460d3bc075720a47b79cd787ac374","1155b1f553206f1689c0adf12feb8586fe41b6cddb1fe82e3bd2ca2aaf6911f3","b770b01e67e03ecabd9cdc855b7ecceaf04839c4ea32c66f3fd336bf86ea2323","bccfb995d6af0034bbfb973b890d19e85c3cae28e97f92c31b3506ffcd25ea4b","fdf69d3bf732b16ac24b05183012a6c6b00bd2a08d7b69cb367d0b3088341e44","93daef8a784ce6409221ceeb1ac10f022d984c51887cc1b1a26ec8babc3a12e1","1f2984c5fceefa0c6a4177d1b9f3dce8709be900067bcb972b1943ea6be8660b","2a8b5440341c9949856ef488f168eee4f136fa1e23758d06acd43675ee45878d","c2e04e05a477f901f2a85af85723916150e52f042a9b3a73bc6ec3de8a3d6f89","8e01af3055cd645d71712bdecc68bb9467cbec2f4bbaa2f583c0a1150d64b5d2"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.15.3L2 U2N or U2U Remote UE Addition/Modification","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if no SRAP entity has been established:","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish a SRAP entity as specified in TS 38.351 [66];","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-L2IdentityRemote value included in the sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList that is not part of the current UE configuration (L2 U2N Remote UE Addition):","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>configure the parameters to SRAP entity in accordance with the sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay;","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if SRB1 is included in sl-MappingToAddModList, and sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 is configured:","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release SL-RLC1, if established;","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>associate the PC5 Relay RLC channel as indicated by sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 with SRB1;","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else: (i.e. SRB1 is not included in sl-MappingToAddModList, or SRB1 is included in sl-MappingToAddModList, but sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 is not configured)","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if SL-RLC1 is not established:","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>apply the default configuration of SL-RLC1 as specified in clause 9.2.4 and associate it with the SRB1;","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-L2IdentityRemote value included in the sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList that is part of the current UE configuration (L2 U2N Remote UE modification):","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>modify the configuration in accordance with the sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay;","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2U Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if no SRAP entity has been established:","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish a SRAP entity as specified in TS 38.351 [66];","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each target L2 U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-L2IdentityRemoteUE value included in the sl-U2U-RemoteUE-ToAddModList that is not part of the current UE configuration (target L2 U2U Remote UE Addition):","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each source L2 U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-SourceUE-Identity in accordance with one entry of the sl-SourceRemoteUE-ToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure the parameters to SRAP entity in accordance with the sl-SRAP-ConfigU2U;","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each target L2 U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-L2IdentityRemote value included in the sl-U2U-RemoteUE-ToAddModList that is part of the current UE configuration (target L2 U2U Remote UE modification):","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each source L2 U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-SourceUE-Identity included in the sl-SourceRemoteUE-ToReleaseList (source L2 U2U Remote UE Release):","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the configuration associated with the source L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"424eb093f767dd650e5338895960519d92ebea981f57d2d92b779f748b231a17","original_member_sha256":"c43941f5cb11f87748367ce8365b9a3c5ac1bf79a9c30e779a91aa0d1036aaf3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b602c8e66e1be699ade9bd39f540253662957b58233b87a09faa086ce2a5c12d","d5ad69c0fbfc5bf639bf63fa94063f2f62b0939db11b275f545e1804985ca858","b1cc51780382f9ed009922d13db568e541cbada864ac51699a28657f68602703","8ffe93d8be640a203e8739ce420045e5818494f2a902c4bf9a5a180fb79c21ec","0b93ff20a114f988274b354cc9c8d8a68243f43e898d725ced664b86971c654b","73ffdb018e4f25c5f9046cb3fccdf11d63dc3326d7ef485346f02e41a6e48729","414f236896483d16ccf7ef6c6089738d901d591eb67afb0bc24ce66f3f062109","20fab542586c554592894ddf485037aac0a5d0bb48607a0d244458c432d7b51b","af3dc3818e5910e686accedc5c3f150f8b2c363f9cd22bef00259f2749df56f3","548d77ca3bd64ee90e58626654f8704d81a82f2508652af8b439a537ad57727d","61a0faa67d72800f3444b02f1f2c4b7e00ceba9f630de3e954776930e69e3093","ef983f617d5bf2b1fa2dfa65491ff95bd56e77373915d18334298d711928a999","c945397f0afba4af0ad61b674f7cf65831bc538cdd654119ea33a6e205897e94","28285d8ee106b4204e5a1079e6d07410b1192d7f34ce7aa93192dd7b968e9f76","516242b97bd9975f7767aa6069c88a9108bc20fa44a74764ab80644a7e70a899","b368f1ad828e1e847bf038b8265936d4a61c57fafffd1ed5211e3f8156165ec8","520109dc445db2f57c5e9f173af203e11e75a808923797f84fe5c488ad5800bc","9082ab499e3c602a388f1fa2311277db10a586a123f9bec52de684d8c09d52ab","bb1545940b788ff353234b7b214d52bacd9ec9a8d5c9691489605a6f88ca049c","babfd95883dcb17dead2a2d4360a19cd1ded7bad8a98bd814b5777c8fd6e1bd0","48423880f58c81d9d878ef80bf628a72bd1617bd84a4e7984f222146cc7f5fe3","959fc6e22f33c9e0e3c5722d20498797dbb366c2c636b41b45899704d151fce5","a947c304a7fd06a264b99b31edc7d5ba2650e0991cdf0a695b9ff9d924cad659","1e6355a402a5b71ceba7b1a9b9fd36de377f510f9311eb089ed668c8942662e9"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for the source L2 U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-SourceUE-Identity included in the sl-SourceRemoteUE-ToAddModList that is not part of the current UE configuration (source L2 U2U Remote UE Addition):","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure the parameters to SRAP entity in accordance with the sl-SRAP-ConfigU2U;","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for the source L2 U2U Remote UE indicated in sl-SourceUE-Identity included in the sl-SourceRemoteUE-ToAddModList that is part of the current UE configuration (source L2 U2U Remote UE modification):","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>modify the configuration in accordance with the sl-SRAP-ConfigU2U;","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1> if sl-FastFailoverConfig is included:","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2> for each (sl-L2IdentityRemote, sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity):","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> store the priority-ordered egress candidates for local egress re-selection upon AS-layer failure on the current egress link.","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.15.3a Local egress re-selection (fast failover) at L2 U2N Relay UE","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When sl-FastFailoverConfig is configured for a (sl-L2IdentityRemote, RB) and the relay detects AS-layer failure (PC5 link failure/release or Uu RLF/release) on the current egress, the relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1> select the highest-priority entry in sl-EgressCandidateList that is not barred and for which lower layers indicate the link is available;","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2> update the egress link and RLC channel used for that (sl-L2IdentityRemote, RB) accordingly;","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> if the selected change modifies the parent as seen by the child UE, submit NotificationMessageSidelink as specified in 5.8.9.10.4; otherwise, no signaling to the child is required;","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4> if no candidate is available, indicate failure to upper layers.","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1: The network may subsequently send RRCReconfiguration; this procedure does not preclude it.","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2: This subclause does not introduce any new on-air headers; it builds on the SRAP mapping model and existing RRC lists for indirectly-connected UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.4Actions related to reception of NotificationMessageSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving the NotificationMessageSidelink, the Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the indicationType is included:","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if MP is configured and MCG transmission (i.e. direct path) is not suspended;","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the indicationType is relayUE-HO;","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"424eb093f767dd650e5338895960519d92ebea981f57d2d92b779f748b231a17","original_member_sha256":"c43941f5cb11f87748367ce8365b9a3c5ac1bf79a9c30e779a91aa0d1036aaf3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8d8563b9c9eb7ff388c470d3c6e3fdae7ae9f10d8e1642f98fc6d6dd86452edc","044d56e6c1766f20ea642619d300855d5ba739ced8092cb1ccc1f7f123a2da47","f7d17e85456c6ce3878be782c4e837df8145f3c4cf5df887862bc13b7b412c61","6c241c817fe35c485d91c7cc2961edb0d6cd6b0b3ddd3e0ed07fdf1d8b418a25","1b0fe21801e4cfb1fdf1a19197fb6d2ea2f0d315b29c953a0b5b80943d2b4101","35d57ed66d48bf1e5c2b7450bcfe29de365d00dbc760c77431b93a00ac1e3046","a4f8c0933bcb13877c59ceb8e63ff00c13bd405ae7d22d86d659273e41cdd1f0","00e9dc80ce5f9153dde434d9046fecd53c7747bcfd6b957824d14822fc4d2563","51eecf313471f46e6ea6e2e14e47a1356eb651cbe4fec1dfca4e9d4f9619a7fc","24267a80db4da2ae38362e0a2771805f1f3e52d6054b430447efa85ac40a116c","ba926ce96749f0a0e0e2a2a5e4b2091a1bffde9fdaa0afaaaec64ac3b3d4086b","33a6a79ffbaa7b91d6803e6eadc32c11aed365c726f38fb71f65d5328c4063c2","31a650f130e82b2e32feb5e9198dd746cc39b6200173d2c479f6b1a8e60f8d68","176988a2144c21b5f246beafc16b7404ef57b7cd2f9c6ea3ec4649222bab53e2","ade6a742aef2cc68333d4bee7480f3f3421f37e59f2cc6bcfe14c6aa26ec9cb5","6e964007c7a3d3a7642f0a12d10f4229b5d7bb721aaef6388f867863ded3e911","c505551ceb8db1301eea9d3ae4e6c4fb9173953ffb714f147b3165b8f20e2fed","3c50a47f016f4c75f1dcea5913d1743ea0a39bf606f98fa610bb68d0ac402b93","e71fd5c98fbd72429543e7c6dfe71c99e13c418fc718370e41b1ab193f5b4362","d5cb55a3f828c4359447a365c450b67696f501d3cb01d2a39c580e9b963d89bd","09fa94b95d43ad65dafd0502643957926329b464e26ac28a019b0ae538250b72","5a7198bcdbe79de192a4d4e0dcd5753b6edb5667a6dd7eb20c157d6a4d4afec3","741eb0ead61f79dbd4a29d190102333cdd4f7bb821e5f8012aa4e8d51fb16d27","f2166b428975279b17a4042636054f62ec9d9f9dbd4a75652393416d213fa87a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2505726.zip::R2-2505726_Fast failover via pre‑configured egress candidate list for multi‑hop L2 U2N relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>suspend indirect path transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else:","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>initiate the indirect path failure information procedure as specified in 5.7.3c to report indirect path failure;","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else if T301 is not running, initiate the RRC connection re-establishment procedure as specified in 5.3.7;","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else (the UE is L3 U2N Remote UE, or L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE):","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the PC5-RRC connection with the U2N Relay UE is determined to be released:","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>indicate upper layers to trigger PC5 unicast link release;","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else (i.e., maintain the PC5 RRC connection):","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is L2 U2N Remote UE and the indicationType is relayUE-HO or relayUE-CellReselection:","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>consider cell re-selection occurs;","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the upstream relay (re)selection is triggered by AS-layer failure and the Remote UE is in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE, further handling is up to upper layers; the UE may keep or release the PC5 link as already specified for Notification handling.","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:For L3 U2N Remote UE, or L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE, it is up to Remote UE implementation whether to release or keep the PC5 unicast link.","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The L2 U2N Remote UE may ignore the NotificationMessageSidelink if it does not release the PC5 unicast link in source side yet during an indirect-to-direct path switch, i.e. T304 is running.","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-IndicationType is relayUE-PC5-RLF:","paragraph_zero_based":206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>indicate PC5 RLF received from L2 U2U Relay UE to the upper layers for the indicated L2 U2U Remote UE based on the received sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the end-to-end PC5 connection failure for the end-to-end PC5 connection(s) over the per-hop PC5 link between the L2 U2U Relay UE and the L2 U2U Remote UE identified by sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the end-to-end PC5 connection failure related actions as specified in 5.8.9.3a;","paragraph_zero_based":209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:It is up to the upper layers on whether to trigger U2U Relay reselection and whether to keep or release the PC5 link with the U2U Relay UE after the PC5 RLF indication received from U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.3.5Sidelink information elements","paragraph_zero_based":212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-L2RelayUE-Config","paragraph_zero_based":213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-L2RelayUE-Config is used to configure L2 U2N relay operation related configurations used by L2 U2N Relay UE, or L2 U2U relay operation related configurations used by L2 U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-L2RelayUE-Config information element","paragraph_zero_based":215}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"424eb093f767dd650e5338895960519d92ebea981f57d2d92b779f748b231a17","original_member_sha256":"c43941f5cb11f87748367ce8365b9a3c5ac1bf79a9c30e779a91aa0d1036aaf3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["bfa117f58f96b1a307594fd511bf6896a02cb99b232f5d6c3d7c7f6e89bcebae","28348ee0a9649bb4f0d6b4c5f4af8b9a7962ff3a2d24821fa02263ea6915c347","1665487c067f2d78b8892048347f0e57baa3b1853f8a2f69725c82a6e5ecb2cb","de71e01ec1792514258e9f51ee06461775c2496ab41ac314162ebf180514c813","d020dd3056117e1b2a67b780f651206ebc0ce754fd14b5ef625e1ad2a35d6c1c","66bda765a8d197a2304eba72a5d02be94a12362dea01243adbe5f3b4a97f4f04","0b674d8deff6753f6c6a157f11130237d208a8b17f506ae54bdc979440a90587","4997d8543a3d63db2c6c27d6e9e809f558e47c1aaa8c55ad08203bccb5527a27","f35ad9cc3a378a15268ed525fedf11288a3b912e9ad309c5b8a1fbd510a9eaf2","902ca47d5faed5ac2ae7a78fe0c553b5e1ba5dc8e5bd96ef7b00d73b979d7dad","30f57a27788006d2a7bd996d037a0921cd530510850baf5fccb2c4e1f1c5443b","cba0cd4eb6b40a4281a9c12b69a8e4c83d1ad6eb4c2e68e8bfb848df39ca43be","39ddbdcb44eeef0d49af261953808f05c542f17c9466b1d76265c81ebc0aad85","5adefdc6114d960be838941a02b91880337a7721af63cfb36e59c2b25b949e70","7edd93ce2e0c6769672cca78a285f82d43c5b0bd58440203ccc03ae5abdcced8","026d65cecf444bdf635c896d45c51f23f4cc89c4554baf01f90e820179d952a9","4b9155caeb0dbab367bf79453bc633badbd862f22f3763f803381d6dfa0f58db","d9790259bd26280bf47b6bddb9d1404aa849e86fa342ba7fc14ea22ba5242865","5b48ff9728e1c463b2cc9aafe5e72c5ec275d2cc12532469fc0cfe4caf94490b","41a97e09313d113d617a5ba07479dbc8bce1b4dc9066038d473091177e5597d3","3f9578212d137fb85615e6de0034bbec9ded7a56922c492b1ca3fe2eafdfc33f","65848611e7b5a5fc007bbaa045f8d480bd3a7113f4b0a242640b7fd270cccc3b","dfc8d825a5f0418792d95c39b226bfe6b22c620dc31d824ece8ccd090c3d4dfc","d54b503da7180c06f12279326b9e21e358c9c3d3b537b9f156e71572