{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2507420.zip::R2-2507420 Correction on AI for Air Interface Feature in TS 37320.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[22]3GPP TS 38.300: \"NR; NR and NG-RAN Overall description; Stage-2\".","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[23]3GPP TS 28.558: \"Management and orchestration; UE level measurements for 5G system\".","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3Definitions, symbols and abbreviations","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.1Definitions","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the terms and definitions given in TR 21.905 [1] apply.","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Immediate MDT: MDT functionality involving measurements performed by the UE in CONNECTED state and reporting of the measurements to RAN available at the time of reporting condition as well as measurements by the network for MDT purposes.","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Logged MDT: MDT functionality involving measurement logging by UE in IDLE mode, INACTIVE state, CELL_PCH, URA_PCH states and CELL_FACH state when second DRX cycle is used (when UE is in UTRA) for reporting to eNB/RNC/gNB at a later point in time, and logging of MBSFN measurements by E-UTRA UE in IDLE and CONNECTED modes.","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Management Based MDT PLMN List: MDT PLMN List applicable to management based MDT.","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MDT measurements: Measurements determined for MDT.","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MDT PLMN List: A list of PLMNs where MDT is allowed for a user. It is a subset of the EPLMN list and RPLMN at the time when MDT is initiated.","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Signalling Based MDT PLMN List: MDT PLMN List applicable to signalling based MDT.","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.2Symbols","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the following symbols apply:","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<symbol><Explanation>","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.3Abbreviations","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the abbreviations given in TR 21.905 [1] and the following apply. An abbreviation defined in the present document takes precedence over the definition of the same abbreviation, if any, in TR 21.905 [1].","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ACKAcknowledgement","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"AICHAcquisition Indicator CHannel","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BLERBlock Error Rate","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BSSIDBasic Service Set Identifier","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CACarrier Aggregation","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CDMACode Division Multiple Access","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CHOConditional Handover","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"0254bea9b44234fd4ae3ce61d1b7572c9739a2f3f98aac5d753159622ecf9743","original_member_sha256":"89d3a65a890ec1c34665df3994d13674a43f65265801792df8571bdbaed4c1df","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["1d2fa836bcf747b004d59106705aa6915552f7e716f62a0eb1e04d126341298b","3049f7d31e49614b8b349e006f333ba7dc8d284c9518abe270492ede29e597c7","2151d4cf28596bf84a6f3d0017d7bc798