{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2507680.zip::R2-2507680 Corrections to AIML for NR air interface.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-LOGGEDMEASUREMENTCONFIGID-START","paragraph_zero_based":4056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-LoggedMeasurementConfigId-r19 ::=            INTEGER (0..maxNrofLoggedMeasurementConfigurations-1-r19)","paragraph_zero_based":4058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-LOGGEDMEASUREMENTCONFIGID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":4060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":4061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CSI-MeasConfig","paragraph_zero_based":4063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CSI-MeasConfig is used to configure CSI-RS (reference signals) belonging to the serving cell in which CSI-MeasConfig is included, channel state information reports to be transmitted on PUCCH on the serving cell in which CSI-MeasConfig is included and channel state information reports on PUSCH triggered by DCI received on the serving cell in which CSI-MeasConfig is included. See also TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2. The IE CSI-MeasConfig is also used to configure logging of channel state information for the serving cell in which CSI-MeasConfig is included, as specified in 5.5x.3.","paragraph_zero_based":4064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-MeasConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":4065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":4066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-MEASCONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":4067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-MeasConfig ::=                  SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":4