{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2507680.zip::R2-2507680 Corrections to AIML for NR air interface.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"minSchedulingOffsetPreferenceConfigExt","paragraph_zero_based":5400},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration for the UE to report assistance information to inform the gNB about the UE's preferred minimumSchedulingOffset value for cross-slot scheduling for power saving for SCS 480 kHz and/or 960 kHz.","paragraph_zero_based":5401},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"minSchedulingOffsetPreferenceProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":5402},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Prohibit timer for preferred minimumSchedulingOffset assistance information reporting. Value in seconds. Value s0 means prohibit timer is set to 0 seconds, value s0dot5 means prohibit timer is set to 0.5 seconds, value s1 means prohibit timer is set to 1 second and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":5403},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"multiRx-PreferenceReportingConfigFR2","paragraph_zero_based":5404},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration for the UE to report assistance information to inform gNB about the UE's preference on multi-Rx operation for FR2.","paragraph_zero_based":5405},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"multiRx-PreferenceReportingConfigFR2ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":5406},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Prohibit timer for multi-Rx operation preference reporting for FR2. Value in seconds. Value s0 means prohibit timer is set to 0 seconds, value s0dot5 means prohibit timer is set to 0.5 seconds, value s1 means prohibit timer is set to 1 second and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":5407},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-CandidateBandList","paragraph_zero_based":5408},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of candidate bands that the network intends to use, e.g., for serving cells and for which the UE is requested to provide information on temporary restricted capabilities for MUSIM operation as specified in clause 5.7.4.3.","paragraph_zero_based":5409},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-GapAssistanceConfig","paragraph_zero_based":5410},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration for the UE to report assistance information for gap preference.","paragraph_zero_based":5411},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-GapPriorityAssistanceConfig","paragraph_zero_based":5412},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the UE is allowed to provide MUSIM assistance information for gap(s) priority and/or MUSIM gaps keep preference.","paragraph_zero_based":5413},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-GapProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":5414},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Prohibit timer for MUSIM assistance information reporting for gap preference.","paragraph_zero_based":5415},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-LeaveAssistanceConfig","paragraph_zero_based":5416},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration for the UE to report assistance information for leaving RRC_CONNECTED for MUSIM purpose.","paragraph_zero_based":5417},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-LeaveWithoutResponseTimer","paragraph_zero_based":5418},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the timer for the UE to enter RRC_IDLE for MUSIM purpose as defined in clause 5.3.8.6.","paragraph_zero_based":5419},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":5420},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the prohibit timer for UE temporary restricted capabilities for MUSIM operation. Value in milliseconds. Value ms0 means prohibit timer is set to 0 milliseconds, value ms10 means prohibit timer is set to 10 milliseconds and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":5421},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"musim-WaitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":5422},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the wait timer for UE temporary restricted capabilities for MUSIM operation. Value in milliseconds. Value ms10 means wait timer is set to 10 milliseconds, value ms20 means wait timer is set to 20 milliseconds and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":5423}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"8ea3f2cd17cc64a7fc93b34e322a9917fea2f6fb2ccc8fd888363f550f5f01ad","original_member_sha256":"a9ae874fc8477ca54ba94d75064a5096273f26d409ca0f0a3ac4dc63a68b1cd6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8fee77f8a8277ef4ec2fde708b1c0cd4cc46982ab621fd348d83dc9802bfcd9f","37849c82221d5e8766e976d3f24e6fd90a4a75441483753b1421c64f8d1fac4e","661dcaf01b8c50cb8311458d94a33647cf9f5d90ffef4993baaebd56c5646650","4fba011c72ff4abb95a73e7c484688e90f693f94a02744a9e61f6307ae2a997c","a65657e9c47adddb7f47e703ec2fb4450c808dcc85420c3769a4bd45ebaa31db","2f1551c735335cfcf98a3dcfa9ef3f3d3e9956925c25cb21864c945912bbc6ff","a11da6a1bba77f157bc145697efb97c38266282b5b9fa903d876d460beaea73b","60d4b4983608bcbb7bc3f2302afd20091d2702fddec759a7765d4f30b331f917","d6b20e5ad22ef60fb8829f1a3dc4699ba112a3139641bc1207d5ae75a13b99f4","850073ed45abc96dfcbc0b99c9067d68b37b5b8acc657e076567731754391bbe","39d018adce8f9c75d1a3159dedd2a4086f519c8cc3e03817412f5dfe993b116f","1f3422a52bfb2bf91d3cc48cf2978afc1e0b70718bd3c6813069e0d80744f2b1","c1f6c15bd744c38a87f52ab7480151a3ca9d4690fc2ba83715023620a06ed64c","db30081a15b38308e2d8ba4f44feb859a44b0e5936786e759d4e0d9c3f6c5ce3","e10f7b93375ca4f28a465c9024b52ae551bc90eb9eb1b0f88a6909123724c126","68e8ab5ea275298e8a1ef658da66971dd21c6ed5c987d90f40779eb9e244f270","8cb044666201f74d6fbb447aa799f69ef071a6fce92041b5d2c540bb2e5eb402","ca01542dc81fa6f67d18c4d2df319738cbf1ac7da88b7d2fb8071ca02d3b243c","aab609ccbba06a099228aa266be20077d91e152750eb566e1b2eadf7f4ce4e92","83287d6c7665fcfa9175266450acd36b8e7f77a1c6c3882b557a2dddf17ad6da","a195e8685cf3437381f320921a18c23d5acfc9fe3c3c760c322cc4b1104aa890","595d9e037323236fe037d97eacbab8d31192f3080042bcf7a45633ac51cf2c61","65bb18a0cc8d9fb85c88a6386e30838dd4901f179c385639fb4b6d5761fa