{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509161.zip::R2-2509161 36331 R19 Misc Rapp.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"voiceOverPS-HS-UTRA-FDD","paragraph_zero_based":5185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether UE supports IMS voice according to GSMA IR.58 profile in UTRA FDD.","paragraph_zero_based":5186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"voiceOverPS-HS-UTRA-TDD128","paragraph_zero_based":5188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether UE supports IMS voice in UTRA TDD 1.28Mcps.","paragraph_zero_based":5189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"widebandPRG-Slot, widebandPRG-Subslot, widebandPRG-Subframe","paragraph_zero_based":5191},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports wideband precoding resource block group size for slot/subslot/subframe operation as specified in TS 36.213 [23].","paragraph_zero_based":5192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"wlan-IW-RAN-Rules","paragraph_zero_based":5194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports RAN-assisted WLAN interworking based on access network selection and traffic steering rules.","paragraph_zero_based":5195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"wlan-IW-ANDSF-Policies","paragraph_zero_based":5197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports RAN-assisted WLAN interworking based on ANDSF policies.","paragraph_zero_based":5198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"wlan-MAC-Address","paragraph_zero_based":5200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the WLAN MAC address of this UE.","paragraph_zero_based":5201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"wlan-PeriodicMeas","paragraph_zero_based":5203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports periodic reporting of WLAN measurements.","paragraph_zero_based":5204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"wlan-ReportAnyWLAN","paragraph_zero_based":5206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports reporting of WLANs not listed in the measObjectWLAN.","paragraph_zero_based":5207}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"bba13f43bf9f9da1510e8bdb4b93207d82d3fbb590e153518aea1c934313854c","original_member_sha256":"d5729ee741f893aa83122cf8a780d8f66a4f43b530a05b8ace1245a510abed95","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c0308f7f889980ef13c7737b11848136019cbe1f69b761fb583c2da311f0d144","a5712d06b282f552edca42c872364c78d00e116525b83427033110804dcac25c","3475cf5567a86763c2c2a563888ed08cdebedf04d43a88e2b54e9a3c6d78d561","28977d414ed32d1d44843a953775bc29008dbfd7b5ea60c0ac60a897545f5e86","a62551f004dba2a46e2407624c273bdb391a6a0db2d09802de06fafeea0c0e59","a39f527e87a6a4c531e3085536d0b9a6ceca720c90b08af7d97ab0e42733c2fa","fb61bcca24912e183bae5568ca42e3ad20cd0897194068f3640e61e7a43d93af","2e33c243482619e4aa995063b65eea6ace1169766ccacfc7d91e283da964cd20","5b05b90aa61bbab421d518717edc85fcc76cbe99ed50336c3ead2442103777c6","bef817126423f79425f1103ed873c51baa35576ad3e0310112aa0f396db223df","b4f56ed1fd3d6daf317e404b59114ecd1c77eb9db34bd02393f31f89b68d664a","07c2b7a1bf9b83e9f514f80c43eaad4e23753d2759c253d6f5cc7093c4e10e16","2e9f243df0a9a1ce0c5fdbec70dc920615c90c29fd419972aae27e0457693c08","d6eed7fcc8ec3f1ed3c67092e0e0203ce73ef7c04b14f20647f1204c62ff12fb","847423664a2f3395e31f67d15d30297272526c6d1933fefb9ae20f2facb4f290","5f1e44a94ecd87cbf4cfcc251a950aa8ace7eb2fb597bd092860fa791636bac9","706b103cd045932d9d4002580ff90ccbb4a9faaadbcd53fc49a41214539c3583","c4e2c100d5d0b6eaff3bf4081caa3daf8eb49c285805380d9bd8f9568a46a76b","9022c884c427dd6969b2620172a743d63b39a549c9cd40f2c30088fc29a454b8","306cf5e15e5691c550f3cdfd491c1e3b1d1aa68c577b48fc8ded8ec420b90c93","eddc40ea9abd56977157273a1dafb4ca1d4e1a302ee5079aa01e35a845139f25","e999cf583c35e637ff1c8ac10d27ee413ec094eb391ed72a8ccd99e17dde0810","83f2e8c812019e4bb67e229e0a74dda6a29a67676d10c0523a6b690f126a0b1f","dede1df4e1ca70952aa4a5f8e6fd64124f0bd4d98f5addeb9570af8677c7fd16"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[5184,5207],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2509161.zip::R2-2509161 36331 R19 Misc Rapp.docx:p5184"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509161.zip::R2-2509161 36331 R19 Misc Rapp.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"wlan-SupportedDataRate","paragraph_zero_based":5209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum WLAN data rate supported by the UE over all LWA bearers. Actual value of supported data rate is field value * 10 Mbps (i.e., value 1 corresponds to 10 Mbps, value 2 corresponds to 20 Mbps and so on). ","paragraph_zero_based":5210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":5211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"zp-CSI-RS-AperiodicInfo","paragraph_zero_based":5212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports aperiodic ZP-CSI-RS transmission for the indicated transmission mode.","paragraph_zero_based":5213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Yes","paragraph_zero_based":5214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":5215},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The IE UE-EUTRA-Capability does not include AS security capability information, since these are the same as the security capabilities that are signalled by NAS. Consequently, AS need not provide \"man-in-the-middle\" protection for the security capabilities.","paragraph_zero_based":5216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The column FDD/ TDD diff indicates if the UE is allowed to signal, as part of the additional capabilities for an XDD mode i.e. within UE-EUTRA-CapabilityAddXDD-Mode-xNM, a different value compared to the value signalled elsewhere within UE-EUTRA-Capability (i.e. the common value, supported for both XDD modes). A '-' is used to indicate that it is not possible to signal different values (used for fields for which the field description is provided for other reasons). Annex E specifies for which TDD and FDD serving cells a UE supporting TDD/FDD CA shall support a capability for which it indicates support within the capability signalling.","paragraph_zero_based":5217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2a:From REL-15 onwards, the UE is not allowed to signal different values for FDD and TDD unless yes is indicated in column FDD/ TDD diff (i.e. no need to introduce field description solely for the purpose of indicate no).","paragraph_zero_based":5218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:The BandCombinationParameters for the same band combination can be included more than once.","paragraph_zero_based":5219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 4:UE CA and measurement capabilities indicate the combinations of frequencies that can be configured as serving frequencies.","paragraph_zero_based":5220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 5:The grouping of the cells to the first and second cell group, as indicated by supportedCellGrouping, is shown in the table below. The leading / leftmost bit of supportedCellGrouping corresponds to the Bit String Position 1.","paragraph_zero_based":5221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Nr of Band Entries:","paragraph_zero_based":5222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5","paragraph_zero_based":5223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4","paragraph_zero_based":5224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3","paragraph_zero_based":5225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Length of Bit-String:","paragraph_zero_based":5226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"15","paragraph_zero_based":5227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7","paragraph_zero_based":5228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3","paragraph_zero_based":5229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Bit String Position","paragraph_zero_based":5230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell grouping option (0= first cell group, 1= second cell group)","paragraph_zero_based":5231}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"bba13f43bf9f9da1510e8bdb4b93207d82d3fbb59