{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509465.zip::R2-2509465.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"referenceAltitudeCoarse","paragraph_zero_based":240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is present if a 3D grid is provided and specifies the coarse altitude, scale factor 10m, of the upmost layer of the grid relative to the WGS84 ellipsoid. If this field is absent, a 2D grid is provided, valid for ground level.","paragraph_zero_based":241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"upperValidityDeltaAltitude","paragraph_zero_based":242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field, if present, specifies the upper validity altitude relative to the grid upper layer altitude. Enumerated values n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n10, n20, n50, n100 correspond to 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100 metres, respectively. If the field is absent, the default value is 0m.","paragraph_zero_based":243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"lowerValidityDeltaAltitude","paragraph_zero_based":244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field, if present, specifies the lower validity altitude relative to the lowest grid layer altitude. Enumerated values n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n10, n20, n50, n100 correspond to 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100 metres, respectively. If the field is absent, the default value is 0m.","paragraph_zero_based":245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[…]","paragraph_zero_based":247},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–NavModel-NavIC-KeplerianSet2","paragraph_zero_based":248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE NavModel-NavIC-KeplerianSet2 is used for NavIC L1 as defined in [55].","paragraph_zero_based":249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NavModel-NavIC-KeplerianSet2-r19 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":252}