ha256":"824a7bac8b90a08f9c293c8307b4f9799ba11ab540515c3a2f934fb64b1eff8e","original_member_sha256":"ea179417e72d27050f309eb5d0934180343e1eb6483f937dc1b0eef874b15949","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["13a296cdc0117fe8fab98180233cab30f64a0cefa9202305e6800261ccf44a19","5a13fceff94c505bcc5a761d985dc17eb1bfcf9724f7626d3bae06c87b37acc0","adbe9aef20714c53b1b69be5e44d99670e19abf9f79e304737f63d509c628f92","7ae559ec2991ca97b15292717e994fec32dd6bb2702fd82d71df5f6d3449fc80","59190e70ece9ffb806e9984eb0949613812c790031ebd2f417b07742101bcec3","5b9d3e94b2e2469a162f36c651ac6802b31fcc4b4fed4f8769f27295b66f32e3","0e47661d68410752894205dee6a9bbbad763c4fb8f938472f606caa30fd5b3b2","d260611a045c20b1b3f9ecdad9ec57a014a998988a464295e1390231dab41ff6","046072d789da32203b2dbdc5bf6faf7ce0947321bf61b1475c3867e7f07b4f28","ad7c58beb1d9e90fb0849bcd216a0fa195ed528b17181f725cf2b49a179cb8f1","826ddaefbd35bf5941dd0ba7402603c67afa4054d718e9bc0124542ef7dca6de","f93659204248bf7212a2a073874fa6ef6bab855e1f334d94d95f69bdfcb0d978","321940f9ecf77394071dc4d0a373495ed9d27c75e97c1678643468bea45f7693","84cfffd8b170c458e9fd1f937758338e77952052a138c7c60120dc1e8ee9c412","f7b3a7bb9ad97a828da3323273c2deac8004729d61d7f2c7a25185dd92d4eb66","623edfeb67c2d41b2b9e147012100dce2f709456a108863b11db12637e74c692","972c89243ea25b912af8179a8be8c77ab6d50347dd064fa94fff2d9d947bbd4b","022031e640f79d734e0c0078695b4546709c7cc0e2d4b09f740c852d83464850","90739a9b5718a75a6036a95b91a37f44f1e9aef38922942dfe97f431acb1a425","6c4b79aee2df9417fdcf7ff053d8ed2a9ea25e31efedf31e6292500ff9c4b627","8a2054446422db10127b53522c244dd671006eed469081cd46119e9103434846","09696b54939497a8ca2ba620420c03c7479c8446d64fb680ae1962b6d211066f","c002616492b1923e46d6fa95a25dac7944411eca88ccdcee2199f265ed726678","d02e8cbd697ae1810074c3012247d88e70339f7889a7482c352e21eca4a8f878"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Start of change","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.1Terms","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the terms given in TR 21.905 [1] and the following apply. A term defined in the present document takes precedence over the definition of the same term, if any, in TR 21.905 [1].","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Child UE: a U2N Relay UE’s next hop in downstream direction for serving a U2N Remote UE in U2N Relay communication. Child UE can be the U2N Remote UE or a U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Downstream: direction toward U2N Remote UE in U2N Relay communication.","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Egress RLC channel: a RLC channel on which a packet is transmitted by a U2N Relay UE, a U2N Remote UE, a U2U Remote UE, a U2U Relay UE or a network node.","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Egress link: a radio link on which a packet is transmitted by a U2N Relay UE, a U2N Remote UE, a U2U Remote UE, a U2U Relay UE or a network node.","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ingress RLC channel: a RLC channel on which a packet is received from a U2N Relay UE, a U2N Remote UE, a U2U Remote UE, a U2U Relay UE or a network node.","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ingress link: a radio link on which a packet is received from a U2N Relay UE, a U2N Remote UE, a U2U Remote UE, a U2U Relay UE or a network node.","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Intermediate U2N Relay UE: a U2N Relay UE having both PC5 connection to a parent UE and PC5 connection to a child UE or a U2N Remote UE for serving the U2N Remote UE in case of multi-hop L2 U2N Relay communication.","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Last U2N Relay UE: a U2N Relay UE having both Uu connection to the network and PC5 connection to a child UE for serving a U2N Remote UE in case of L2 U2N Relay communication. The child UE is the U2N Remote UE in case of single-hop L2 U2N Relay communication.","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parent UE: a U2N Remote UE or U2N Relay UE’s next hop U2N Relay UE in upstream direction for serving the U2N Remote UE in U2N Relay communication.","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2N Relay UE: a UE that provides functionality to support connectivity to the network for U2N Remote UE(s). Up to three L2 U2N Relay UEs (i.e., one Last U2N Relay and up to two Intermediate U2N Relays including one First U2N Relay) can be configured for serving a L2 U2N Remote UE in multi-hop L2 U2N Relay communication in this release.","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2N Remote UE: a UE that communicates with the network via one or more U2N Relay UEs on an indirect path.","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2U Relay UE: a UE that provides functionality to support connectivity between two U2U Remote UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2U Remote UE: a UE that communicates with other UE(s) via a U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE-to-Network Relay communication: a mode of communication in which a UE communicates with the network through an indirect path involving only one U2N Relay UE for single-hop L2 U2N Relay communication or multiple L2 U2N Relay UEs for multi-hop L2 U2N Relay communication.","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upstream: direction toward gNB in U2N Relay communication.","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2.2SRAP entities","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.2-1 represents one possible structure for the SRAP sublayer. The figure is based on the radio interface protocol architecture defined in TS 38.300 [2].","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.2-1: SRAP structure overview","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"824a7bac8b90a08f9c293c8307b4f9799ba11ab540515c3a2f934fb64b1eff8e","original_member_sha256":"ea179417e72d27050f309eb5d0934180343e1eb6483f937dc1b0eef874b15949","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["5e6e78c509901ae3936d881dd0c9b12c94a02c1a5b9226ba72b61bcdd6bc46b1","7e893fbf424f8ccfb0192c00fbfe778b883e3f04f4f73394dd558cf37301125f","ae8a8be9aa6a7d3a41816f0a784340fc991a959f05c0ba45af2158809f20d96b","4ce8e38d80b5d7ea8330b36f2a3d97f1f83913c44a3a7f612050756ff0307952","494a7ef17a2510a6b1f2a2ab2b694ae0273f85a5ffa5c9ea3ee36b6cdbe2bd38","0dd4e728e5d03435233f8700430735fa7dfc1084a5fe9c282cb23097daf3a291","4a3a86f5d7b2888e91c4c39fbac1a481a44e4825bc0ec8b84e6be10186c95b68","768b49e4f09a18961920f368cd6bb8227146132ebfa60e45fd0ff5936d6c7381","b490c7c8ee9b2eedb655309c850fca2e0720e68f67dbe71564eb11bb77ba196e","f649274c062deba9e04dcd4c0b6a51d283b218d508aa1cf2549bd5236825b2a0","68c1af6b3a5c0da5197f2982411640474df4018720fdaad22e51a5480b39e071","ca80ee203b1b2d696cc683ae8856209bba42d59589b4527b8dd5a63677523c6e","05669171f58c4619a24a8d6c4ba505228e3ab59dba7a7d97f11e4fb1bbee9399","816733a1b9e8a72ee44bd806f2931488c5dfc5b738cff64441104eac799ef6f4","d4f0d465cadbb9d4c75c092be184431503ec089f3883e757410fa498bc37c967","dbac225db7e976beda944155c9fa55d66625e820a749e2cc2773a2b2a0a1cd4d","099cd1d673bea1b2d45b412bde27f3a2cf9ec538af3bfb86fd77ac70492a8c8c","810167fc10764692a011e5857d8495df32ee856333f0f23ddad4c16652aa39b9","9053cf1627f68f09cc06fa81b6aaf8c240117d94979024036543306311aab4f4","c10edd8579438fd0986a0828e7e15e2d5adf42c93b395e86c06d7204607a9a9c","b7dabf2908468c6b78d0a0cd496eaa975ee89101e8acfdf7d143afece8a68a13","8dd77d1bdd26cdee920d9d024e8f17ba1827d88f455fe3fd5a4dcd02ac27caa6","d513d46ee794b7f0cc15f2e5501a17d5dcc6e93df9a25bde6de7c05caf24c2be","99c744fbde2f91c2a1fe135a61f005fa632adca318f7e2a291c6dc313fda34ee"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"On the U2N Relay UE in single-hop U2N Relay and the last Relay UE in multi-hop U2N Relay, the SRAP sublayer contains one SRAP entity at Uu interface and a separate collocated SRAP entity at the PC5 interface. On the U2N Remote UE and intermediate Relay UE, the SRAP sublayer contains only one SRAP entity at the PC5 interface. On the U2U Relay UE and U2U Remote UE, the SRAP sublayer contains only one SRAP entity at the PC5 interface.","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Each SRAP entity has a transmitting part and a receiving part. Across the PC5 interface in the U2N case, the transmitting part of the SRAP entity at the U2N Remote UE has a corresponding receiving part of an SRAP entity at the U2N Relay UE, and vice versa. Across the Uu interface, the transmitting part of the SRAP entity at the U2N Relay UE has a corresponding receiving part of an SRAP entity at the gNB, and vice versa.","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Across the PC5 interface in the U2U case, the transmitting part of the SRAP entity at the U2U Remote UE has a corresponding receiving part of an SRAP entity at the U2U Relay UE, and vice versa.","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Across the PC5 interface in the multi-hop U2N relay case, the transmitting part of the SRAP entity at each UE has a corresponding receiving part of an SRAP entity at the Parent UE, and vice versa.","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.2-2 and Figure 4.2.2-3 represents the functional view of the SRAP entity in U2N Relay case for the SRAP sublayer at PC5 interface and at Uu interface respectively. Figure 4.2.2-4 represents the functional view of the SRAP entity in U2U Relay case for the SRAP sublayer at PC5 interface.","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.2-2: Example of functional view of SRAP sublayer at PC5 interface in U2N Relay case","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.2-3: Example of functional view of SRAP sublayer at Uu interface","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In the example of Figure 4.2.2-2 and Figure 4.2.2-3, at relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For data packet not corresponding to SRB0 of the Child UE, the receiving part on the SRAP entity of Uu or PC5 interface delivers SRAP Data PDUs to the transmitting part on the collocated SRAP entity of PC5 interface for DL data packets, and the receiving part on the SRAP entity of PC5 interface delivers SRAP Data PDUs to the transmitting part on the collocated SRAP entity of Uu or PC5 interface for UL data packets. As an alternative, the receiving part may deliver SRAP SDUs to the transmitting part on the collocated SRAP entity. When passing SRAP SDUs, the receiving part removes the SRAP header and the transmitting part of the relay UE adds the SRAP header with the same SRAP header content as carried on the SRAP Data PDU header prior to removal. Passing SRAP SDUs in this manner is therefore functionally equivalent to passing SRAP Data PDUs, in implementation. The following specification therefore refers to the passing of SRAP data packets.","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For UL data packet corresponding to SRB0 of the Child UE, the receiving part on the SRAP entity of PC5 interface delivers SRAP SDUs to the transmitting part on the collocated SRAP entity of Uu or PC5 interface, and the transmitting part on the SRAP entity of Uu or PC5 interface adds the SRAP header in accordance with clause 5.3.3.","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For DL data packet corresponding to SRB0 of the Child UE, the receiving part on the SRAP entity of Uu or PC5 interface delivers SRAP Data PDUs to the transmitting part on the collocated SRAP entity of PC5 interface, and the transmitting part on the SRAP entity of PC5 interface removes the SRAP header in accordance with clause 5.2.2. As an alternative for handling DL data packet corresponding to SRB0 not shown in Figure 4.2.2-2 or Figure 4.2.2-3, the receiving part on the SRAP entity of Uu or PC5 interface removes the SRAP header and delivers SRAP SDUs to the transmitting part on the collocated SRAP entity of PC5 interface.","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.2-4: Example of functional view of SRAP sublayer at PC5 interface in U2U Relay case","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In the example of Figure 4.2.2-4, at U2U relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For U2U data packet, the receiving part on the SRAP entity of PC5 interface between the U2U Relay UE and the U2U Remote UE delivers U2U SRAP Data PDUs to the transmitting part on the SRAP entity of PC5 interface between the U2U Relay UE and the peer U2U Remote UE. As an alternative, the receiving part may deliver SRAP SDUs to the transmitting part on the SRAP entity. When passing SRAP SDUs, the receiving part removes the SRAP header and the transmitting part of the relay UE adds the SRAP header with the same SRAP header content as carried on the U2U SRAP Data PDU header prior to removal. Passing SRAP SDUs in this manner is therefore functionally equivalent to passing U2U SRAP Data PDUs, in implementation. The following specification therefore refers to the passing of SRAP data packets.","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.2Transmitting operation of U2N Relay UE","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.2.0General","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The transmitting part of the SRAP entity on the PC5 interface of U2N Relay UE receives SRAP data packets from the receiving part of the SRAP entity on the Uu or PC5 interface of the same U2N Relay UE, and construct SRAP Data PDUs as needed (see clause 4.2.2).","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the transmitting part of the SRAP entity on the PC5 interface has an SRAP Data PDU to transmit, the transmitting part of the SRAP entity on the PC5 interface shall:","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress link in accordance with clause 5.2.2.1;","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress RLC channel in accordance with clause 5.2.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"824a7bac8b90a08f9c293c8307b4f9799ba11ab540515c3a2f934fb64b1eff8e","original_member_sha256":"ea179417e72d27050f309eb5d0934180343e1eb6483f937dc1b0eef874b15949","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ef1e291c4e7c0c1f3d3374fdf151f6f0dd8f6ed619581664a80cbd886b19a011","f35c28bd4b140d0897818106b99770352238188225e8f357129af9cee6b33485","866b25936353d2c75c48e4012b0f6b81952dde8558895b45f83ce8b4ca4d86e1","171717a58eb4ab487779acb2b8b4671417b8935deedc2b05e88fb6faad50622f","ed568984790a132d64f7df5f56aa1bcb163c8c361d07798847e265759c3c6d8f","092ef930d7a169d110bb02453e810ec22b4009b7152c680c918f546467c564e6","9f63591c6d12902a16bcbca7ccb687939b5ab58da113735bc6cca99186e43f40","91df38f93820670873d53f13a62ab17d863039fe48910b16c772c23816ec9c27","78289ecb74a6ab8ac2c436a7d7cdbe747383b5717dddb1b1d4b59f4b7d105b8c","0e835607c329d6235fa2ce51ed3b6545f28df866719cf7722e56223dda677dfc","cb31ac79e499184d0a9006c49be18c3031f1bc046e1d0bf8c521a781fa87ff86","dee6f8bc20072df2fafcd9d1d44a8109da2212e96c722a5b0025c9b44007bf2a","4b69d6ea91b01f3c72014db109fd3053120ef7c738b2865d3f633c0c0695f4b7","d0123bb28deb0bb0fd658dc3c3c66b296bd76ef7d1f872cdc5aea3e49060a228","6fb6a10806d5b8a52e1cb36b50c35f1286fff405cb6b1b61bb6a639b0c8d7b88","e4902bbbca8332537e5a8dd4260bfd6cd6bcccaf2d3da4ae7367bb1682a7ae49","c896ff6fb1c87270204933e53a68446d5788ffbe266c28a93f54d42a3b37676a","1edf6f31486c04a68a853e866394b0a1d07f85287efa69b203981f38eeb3a498","8d8482595420f9ee7856c172020747c1e6af648c647be7b277bcab7e7dd5847b","46b364871b6cf4d36da715e4ecfdc21317c3c1f5bb0b75380133438e1f35828f","da2b81d58aa6928b4bab8643e434e4709fee27f9fc579166e6fd9da268833e5a","9ccec6f5d9dbc9b27cad3ae80829b90cc30469cbab7afa7cf13b66ef89144f35","5707d56f6e0067603916ba8b9e1b179660b80b8129cb9ce4ddff20cb7e70d67c","d576b4a285990f1870d7a37df3c8caae0cef280b54c9da1cf0520abe5a4d7f09"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the SRAP Data PDU is for SRB0 of the Child UE (for single-hop U2N Relay case, the BEARER ID field is 0, and the bearer is identified as SRB based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing the sl-EgressRLC-ChannelUu which matches the LCID of the Uu Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received; or for multi-hop U2N Relay, the UE ID field matches the sl-LocalIdentity configured in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay, BEARER ID field is 0, and the bearer is identified as SRB based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing either the sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL which matches the LCID of the PC5 Relay RLC Channel or the sl-EgressRLC-Channel-Uu which matches the LCID of the Uu Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received ):","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Remove the SRAP header from the SRAP Data PDU;","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Submit this SRAP Data PDU to the determined egress RLC channel of the determined egress link.","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.2.1Egress link determination","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For a SRAP Data PDU to be transmitted, SRAP entity shall:","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If there is an entry in sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList, whose sl-LocalIdentity included in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay or sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay-ToAddModList matches the UE ID field in SRAP Data PDU:","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress link on PC5 interface corresponding to sl-L2IdentityRemote configured for the concerned sl-LocalIdentity as specified in TS 38.331 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.2.2Egress RLC channel determination","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For a SRAP Data PDU to be transmitted, the SRAP entity shall:","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the SRAP Data PDU is for SRB0 of the Child UE (for single-hop U2N Relay case, the BEARER ID field is 0 and the bearer is identified as SRB based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing the sl-EgressRLC-ChannelUu which matches the LCID of the Uu Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received; or for multi-hop U2N Relay case, the UE ID field matches the sl-LocalIdentity configured in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay, BEARER ID field is 0, and the bearer is identified as SRB based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing either the sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL which matches the LCID of the PC5 Relay RLC Channel or the sl-EgressRLC-Channel-Uu which matches the LCID of the Uu Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received):","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress PC5 Relay RLC channel in the determined egress link corresponding to logicalChannelIdentity for SL-RLC0 as specified in TS 38.331 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else if there is an entry in sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList, whose sl-LocalIdentity included in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay or sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay-ToAddModList matches the UE ID field in SRAP Data PDU, which includes an sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity that matches the SRB identity or DRB identity of the SRAP Data PDU determined by the BEARER ID field (For the BEARER ID shared by both SRB and DRB, SRB and DRB are differentiated based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing the sl-EgressRLC-ChannelUu which matches the LCID of the Uu Relay RLC Channel or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL which matches the LCID of the PC5 Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received, and for DRB, the DRB identity is BEARER ID plus 1):","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the SRAP Data PDU is for SRB1 but the corresponding sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 is absent in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-DL in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay-ToAddModList is absent:","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress PC5 Relay RLC channel in the determined egress link corresponding to logicalChannelIdentity for SL-RLC1 as specified in TS 38.331 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else:","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress PC5 Relay RLC channel in the determined egress link corresponding to sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-DL configured for the concerned sl-LocalIdentity and concerned sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity as specified in TS 38.331 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.3Receiving operation of U2N Remote UE","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving an SRAP Data PDU from lower layer, the receiving part of the SRAP entity shall:","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the SRAP Data PDU is not for SRB0 (not received from SL-RLC0 as specified in TS 38.331 [3]):","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the SRAP Data PDU is received from SL-RLC1 as specified in TS 38.331 [3]:","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Remove the SRAP header of this SRAP Data PDU and deliver the SRAP SDU to PDCP entity of SRB1 by ignoring the UE ID field and BEARER ID field of this SRAP Data PDU;","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else:","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Remove the SRAP header of this SRAP Data PDU and deliver the SRAP SDU to upper layer entity corresponding to the BEARER ID field of this SRAP Data PDU (For the BEARER ID shared by both SRB and DRB, SRB and DRB are differentiated based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing the sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 which matches LCID of the PC5 Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received, and for DRB, the DRB identity is BEARER ID plus 1);","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"824a7bac8b90a08f9c293c8307b4f9799ba11ab540515c3a2f934fb64b1eff8e","original_member_sha256":"ea179417e72d27050f309eb5d0934180343e1eb6483f937dc1b0eef874b15949","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["fea289653bcd1b2b87693a7366cff90f76db54542c8a8751b83881e96c3ed9ba","350a3d673a029912eb04a84c90f7c06766783e74bed5c29cc70a434b416c640a","32a6628626531a35f7c6cd10999ab5d4dd341c56e20fdb8bea1bbcbe75494430","dafe1d7a10cb2d33b31b852ff0756651376e14fc10f5ab400d2d9f8ad7e976bf","35195cfd8d55267a5a2a80dc925edb0c6efedfdd5bd186aa2bd65c02df4853a0","144fa00006535dfa914593833ab128d592f6ce02a874665857e7dd54b6734bb4","3f9191965db5757dc522f9ef94826f4b9bd6fd342a48224377cd76c76b1d2b7f","958e1c01a4e4b1432141ac3262c1a61f60de698d6e178b4d05fa55f1610280d9","ae7d19412f6b6872c505258b0e275e15bf8a63b3837581bf809f9bcc059533f2","f69a6b3a8baf948b2d820896823b8645eb474407c8afde6224c310e7d8c145bc","1cf5a1dd11c90452a13e3f8cd35bb73e0a725989120d4577fd3214db8a1707fe","8ad7662f989cf7707eb5512215447a4571fc5c52ec10804cd8364b9639d9b03b","207b2d6365c448175269824c656b3de4ce02bb53e35f10d0c4981345c9f1a59e","a5ad7f1affbe82344a5afb441e2f6152fb41e91062decb8c05d09d82597e4698","9e4db09e7aed7fcb442b7723f5ad3df15a3b62b7ca1ff3adf8018eb91f151166","43e28742a19140e04d29f662e4d40b5a9bf8207d919e1233ad1b75573ea83bb8","ba2a834257a2bb1c7f4670685d68571434fc6398cf3de00afafb8f8148f78e0c","1de19590e3f8e80582f8b39887c3462621b3a2cf157b0431faca8a94b546d3fd","2c2fed0790bbb37999e01e625ac36985c88881dc21288c4c55bfa2ab506ffedf","09a6d763c78df80a73f9bf8d80a599b83cc74033d2e04fed742b8266f1003cea","cbd4984166bcd5092a11bf8e73a56d482a1e19f59006254d759febba51bec3f8","fbf241a0ee8a49227a6b071332f9cc6ab5e2cb9a8cfa574a59744a00c4ceb575","8b536daca838b2356fe75d057c37c0631d90a82a050536cef653cf8e1f0b3dac","af2cf2334bddc333f1691eb1eda7a53b7041494d2928b720d30fd58beaca37c3"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else:","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Deliver the SRAP SDU (i.e., same as SRAP PDU for SRB0) to upper layer, i.e., RRC layer entity (TS 38.331 [3]).","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.3.2Egress RLC channel determination","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For a SRAP Data PDU to be transmitted, the SRAP entity shall:","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If there is an entry in sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList, whose sl-LocalIdentity included in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay or sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay-ToAddModList matches the UE ID field in SRAP Data PDU:","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the SRAP Data PDU is for SRB0:","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress Uu/PC5 Relay RLC channel corresponding to sl-EgressRLC-ChannelUu or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL configured for SRB0 for the concerned sl-LocalIdentity as specified in TS 38.331 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else if the SRAP Data PDU is received from SL-RLC1 as specified in TS 38.331 [3]:","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress Uu/PC5 Relay RLC channel corresponding to sl-EgressRLC-ChannelUu or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL configured for SRB1 for the concerned sl-LocalIdentity as specified in TS 38.331 [3]. Or determine the egress PC5 Relay RLC channel corresponding to logicalChannelIdentity for SL-RLC1 as specified in TS 38.331 [3] if the corresponding sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL is absent in sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay-ToAddModList.","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Else if there is an entry in sl-RemoteUE-ToAddModList which includes an sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity matches SRB identity or DRB identity of the SRAP Data PDU determined by the BEARER ID field (For the BEARER ID shared by both SRB and DRB, SRB and DRB are differentiated based on sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity associated with the entry containing the sl-EgressRLC-ChannelPC5 or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-DL which matches LCID of the PC5 Relay RLC Channel from which the SRAP Data PDU is received, and for DRB, the DRB identity is BEARER ID plus 1):","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Determine the egress Uu/PC5 Relay RLC channel corresponding to sl-EgressRLC-ChannelUu or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL configured for the concerned sl-LocalIdentity and concerned sl-RemoteUE-RB-Identity as specified in TS 38.331 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"End of change","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":205}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"824a7bac8b90a08f9c293c8307b4f9799ba11ab540515c3a2f934fb64b1eff8e","original_member_sha256":"ea179417e72d27050f309eb5d0934180343e1eb6483f937dc1b0eef874b15949","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["3154cba777d7642c209c88ba1dcffefd48925bb5a91d5242102dfff4766e9f56","6b9a1148781d6cc96d8bd067476ac3529683c092c7503aa4908c149ff3e66ce6","d15c823013365b5d9ae5c8b319a37ff6ebecdb5c280f426f754ccef5eff873ac","7bf73b93f46fd4a0531e7e466029c211d5632572b294199ecb82f684fcc9233c","9a909850a2cd2a954b510408b9fcd2b4a0d0c03e313f7ea179b06e95e111bc1b","627c652d100e77b9d75c46dc0c7d4bf3d0f80109a686833d0698c41b65f74bf6","d304ce1a3a4f07fa1e856124b9debb9cf58b4005c6c7ea525ea46e3b8a32a3b9","5974f21d11ce5d0e3b5a07774e31b8fdb6fb76b2d1998d30f062e5ce8d20dd44","d512ca68145b39a685f62734223787cb9b9ce10008506bed5a47679c88be20da","9aa7d4d0a729805508075fa9e61e78653296f39dc4dddbb9213eb7f094ca153c","e986130ffe0ca1bab7719665cd6b8d4de088d4726f23230398eb4447c55c9447","4d1d0f0a95c5dc8caff9e3e05527dd7e6e5ed4d1722c842c22b5032c52eb9f6b","c05118f2dcb03c9644041ba6c7c9422a37c4804c3bddb6a1ab8e2352a48a3fab","eb3b43f4fd27e6953b84ee0a15b948b51bd8df07a26c5f1e5e84e414279a178f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[192,205],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2509471.zip::R2-2509471.docx:p192"}
